/* 124 original applied cases. Source references locate topics; no official-exam calibration. */
const COVERAGE_OPERATIONAL_LIQUIDITY=[{"id":"b125","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-1.1","reading":"ORR-1","concept":"Risk boundaries and legal loss","question":"A bank loses a lawsuit because staff processed client instructions incorrectly. The risk owner wants to exclude the payment from operational risk because it is a legal expense. Which treatment is most appropriate?","choices":["Include the operational loss and identify the process failure.","Record only a legal-risk exposure outside the operational-risk framework.","Allocate the payment to credit risk because it reduces available capital.","Omit the original event if an insurance recovery is expected."],"answer":0,"explanation":"La perte juridique provient ici d’un processus défaillant : elle relève du risque opérationnel. La nature comptable de la charge ne supprime pas la cause opérationnelle.","why":["Relie correctement la perte à sa cause.","Le risque juridique peut faire partie du périmètre opérationnel.","L’effet sur le capital ne transforme pas la cause en risque de crédit.","La récupération ne supprime pas la perte brute ni le besoin de suivi."],"cue":"Classer selon la cause et le périmètre.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b126","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-1.2","reading":"ORR-1","concept":"Internal versus external fraud","question":"A bank employee deliberately changes supplier bank details and directs a payment to an account the employee controls. Which Basel event category best fits the primary event?","choices":["External fraud.","Internal fraud.","Business disruption and system failures.","Damage to physical assets."],"answer":1,"explanation":"La participation intentionnelle d’un salarié au détournement constitue une fraude interne. Un canal de paiement informatique ne transforme pas la cause en panne de système.","why":["La fraude implique ici une personne interne.","L’auteur interne agit intentionnellement.","Aucune panne n’est décrite.","Aucun dommage physique n’est décrit."],"cue":"Identifier l’auteur et son intention.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b127","topic":"operational","skill":"o-measure","objective":"ORR-1.3","reading":"ORR-1","concept":"Sparse tails and annual averages","question":"A bank records thousands of small processing errors but only one very large conduct settlement in a decade. Why is estimating next-year operational tail loss from the sample mean alone particularly weak?","choices":["The mean is unusable mainly because small errors were observed too frequently.","The conduct settlement should be excluded unless an identical event is expected next year.","Rare severe events and changing exposures are poorly represented by the mean.","The mean is adequate once every processing error is given the same weight as the settlement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"La moyenne ne décrit pas la queue. Des pertes rares, des expositions changeantes et une collecte historique limitée rendent l’extrapolation particulièrement fragile.","why":["Le problème principal est la représentation des pertes rares et du risque futur, pas la fréquence élevée en soi.","Une perte rare reste informative sans répétition à l’identique.","Sépare fréquence courante et incertitude de queue.","La moyenne ne devient pas un quantile de queue par un choix de pondération uniforme."],"cue":"Ne pas confondre moyenne et perte extrême.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b128","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-2.1","reading":"ORR-2","concept":"Board oversight of framework","question":"An operational-risk framework exists, but the board has never reviewed its effectiveness. Management argues the risk function approved it. What is the strongest governance response?","choices":["Delegate all board accountability permanently to the CRO.","Let internal audit set all business risk limits without board involvement.","Replace operational controls with a larger capital budget.","Require board oversight and periodic review of the framework."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le conseil doit exercer une surveillance du dispositif ; l’approbation par la fonction risques ne remplace pas sa responsabilité de gouvernance.","why":["La délégation ne supprime pas la responsabilité du conseil.","L’audit fournit une assurance indépendante plutôt que diriger les limites.","Le capital n’assure pas l’efficacité du contrôle.","Rétablit la surveillance attendue."],"cue":"Le conseil surveille le dispositif.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b129","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-2.2","reading":"ORR-2","concept":"Escalation to risk committee","question":"A business repeatedly breaches operational tolerance and misses remediation deadlines. Which report is most useful for the board risk committee?","choices":["Exposure against appetite, repeat breaches, accountable owners and overdue actions.","Only the current month operating profit.","A list of every ticket without prioritization.","A statement that all issues belong to internal audit."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le comité a besoin d’une vue de l’exposition par rapport à l’appétit, des récurrences et de la responsabilité des actions. Un volume brut de tickets masque les décisions à prendre.","why":["Permet une surveillance et des décisions ciblées.","Le résultat ne décrit pas les dépassements.","Trop de détails non hiérarchisés masquent les enjeux.","Les responsables métiers restent propriétaires des risques."],"cue":"Relier dépassement, responsable et action.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b130","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-2.4","reading":"ORR-2","concept":"Incentives and risk culture","question":"A sales unit meets a zero-loss operational target by discouraging staff from reporting near misses. What change best strengthens risk culture?","choices":["Reward low incident counts without further checks.","Reward timely reporting and remediation, while monitoring conduct outcomes.","Remove independent challenge of sales incentives.","Prohibit anonymous reporting to protect the unit reputation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Un objectif fondé seulement sur le nombre déclaré crée un biais de sous-déclaration. Valoriser l’alerte et la correction rend l’information et les comportements plus fiables.","why":["Renforce le biais de dissimulation.","Aligne les incitations avec la transparence et la maîtrise.","Réduit le contrôle sur les incitations.","Décourage les alertes utiles."],"cue":"Une bonne culture fait remonter les incidents.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b131","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-3.1","reading":"ORR-3","concept":"Top-down and bottom-up identification","question":"A bank has strong process-level RCSAs but missed a strategic shift to dependence on one cloud provider. Which addition most directly addresses the blind spot?","choices":["Repeat the same process questionnaires more often.","Remove process-level assessments entirely.","Add an enterprise-wide dependency and scenario review across business units.","Count historical losses only within each department."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Une analyse transversale complète les évaluations locales : elle révèle les dépendances communes et les concentrations invisibles dans chaque processus isolé.","why":["La fréquence seule ne corrige pas le périmètre.","Les deux approches sont utiles.","Ajoute une perspective globale complémentaire.","L’historique départemental peut masquer la dépendance commune."],"cue":"Compléter le terrain par la vue d’ensemble.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b132","topic":"operational","skill":"o-measure","objective":"ORR-3.2","reading":"ORR-3","concept":"Extreme-risk workshop design","question":"A scenario workshop rejects a prolonged payment outage because it has never occurred internally. What is the best improvement?","choices":["Restrict scenarios to last-year internal losses.","Set loss to zero whenever no frequency estimate exists.","Assign every imagined scenario equal probability.","Use severe plausible scenarios, external experience and dependency analysis."],"answer":3,"explanation":"L’absence de précédent interne n’exclut pas un risque extrême. Des scénarios sévères plausibles, éclairés par des événements externes et les dépendances, améliorent l’identification sans inventer une précision probabiliste.","why":["Élimine justement les risques rares.","L’absence d’estimation ne prouve pas l’absence de risque.","L’imagination ne justifie pas l’équiprobabilité.","Élargit l’identification avec des preuves pertinentes."],"cue":"Rare ne signifie pas impossible.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b133","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-3.4","reading":"ORR-3","concept":"Taxonomy levels and double counting","question":"Two units classify the same failed trade at different taxonomy depths: one uses a broad Level 1 category, the other a detailed Level 3 event. How should group reporting proceed?","choices":["Maintain one event identifier and map the detailed category to its parent levels.","Count the event twice because the labels differ.","Force every event into the external-fraud category.","Delete the detailed category to prevent all analysis below Level 1."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Les niveaux hiérarchiques décrivent la même famille d’événements avec une granularité différente. Un identifiant unique et une remontée vers les parents évitent le double comptage.","why":["Respecte la hiérarchie et l’unicité de l’événement.","Les niveaux ne créent pas deux pertes.","La fraude n’est pas établie.","On peut conserver la granularité sans doubler les événements."],"cue":"Une perte, plusieurs niveaux de lecture.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b134","topic":"operational","skill":"o-measure","objective":"ORR-4.1","reading":"ORR-4","concept":"Gross loss and delayed recovery","question":"A processing incident creates a gross loss of EUR 1.2m. An insurer reimburses EUR 0.4m six months later. For loss-data analysis, what is the most useful recording approach?","choices":["Replace the original event by a single EUR 0.8m amount and discard dates.","Record gross loss and recovery separately, linked to the event and their dates.","Record EUR 1.6m as the gross loss.","Delete the loss once the insurer pays."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Distinguer la perte brute et la récupération conserve la sévérité de l’événement, le risque de délai et la traçabilité. Le net seul masque ces informations.","why":["Le montant net efface le profil et le délai de récupération.","Conserve les informations utiles sans double comptage.","La récupération ne s’ajoute pas à la perte brute.","Une récupération partielle n’annule pas l’incident."],"cue":"Séparer perte brute et récupération.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b135","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-4.3","reading":"ORR-4","concept":"KRI versus control indicator","question":"A manager tracks the percentage of privileged-access reviews completed on time. What does this measure primarily assess?","choices":["The realized monetary loss distribution.","A pure profitability KPI unrelated to controls.","A key control indicator, because it measures execution of a control.","A capital ratio required by Basel."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le taux de réalisation à temps renseigne l’exécution d’un contrôle : c’est un KCI. Il ne démontre toutefois pas à lui seul que la revue est de bonne qualité.","why":["Il ne mesure pas les pertes.","Aucun objectif de profit n’est mesuré.","Mesure bien l’exécution du contrôle.","Il ne mesure pas le capital réglementaire."],"cue":"Mesurer un contrôle ne mesure pas directement une perte.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b136","topic":"operational","skill":"o-measure","objective":"ORR-4.5","reading":"ORR-4","concept":"Fault tree common-event accounting","question":"A loss occurs if either independent control failure A or B occurs. P(A)=2% and P(B)=3%. Under an OR gate, what is the loss-event probability?","choices":["0.06%","6.00%","5.00%","4.94%"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Pour deux événements indépendants, P(A ou B)=0,02+0,03−0,02×0,03=4,94 %. Il faut retrancher l’intersection comptée deux fois.","why":["Calcule seulement l’intersection.","Multiplie à tort la somme par un facteur.","Additionne sans retrancher le chevauchement.","Applique correctement l’union avec intersection."],"cue":"OR : additionner puis retirer l’intersection.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*(.02+.03-.02*.03)","value":4.94,"optionValue":4.94,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b137","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-5.2","reading":"ORR-5","concept":"Preventive versus detective control","question":"A bank wants to prevent one employee from creating and approving a supplier payment. Which control most directly addresses that mechanism?","choices":["Mandatory independent approval before release.","A dashboard counting total payments.","An annual review after payment completion.","Insurance that reimburses some future losses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Une séparation créateur-approbateur avant émission est préventive. Une revue ultérieure détecte le problème après exposition et l’assurance ne bloque pas le paiement.","why":["Bloque l’auto-approbation avant décaissement.","Mesure l’activité sans empêcher le conflit.","Détecte après coup.","Transfère une partie des conséquences, pas la cause."],"cue":"Placer le contrôle avant le décaissement.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b138","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-5.3","reading":"ORR-5","concept":"Automation and systematic failure","question":"An automated reconciliation is introduced. The same developer changes source mapping and approves the production release. Which residual risk deserves priority?","choices":["Automation eliminates the need for segregation of duties.","A systematic mapping error can pass through an unchallenged release.","Only random manual typing errors remain.","The control cannot fail if it runs daily."],"answer":1,"explanation":"L’automatisation peut diffuser une erreur systématique. Une validation indépendante du mapping, des tests et une séparation des droits de mise en production restent nécessaires.","why":["L’automatisation ne supprime pas les conflits de fonctions.","Identifie un défaut susceptible d’affecter tous les rapprochements.","Le risque de conception peut dominer le risque de saisie.","La fréquence d’exécution ne prouve pas l’exactitude."],"cue":"Automatique ne signifie pas validé.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b139","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-5.5","reading":"ORR-5","concept":"New-product approval timing","question":"A bank launches instant payments before testing sanctions screening at peak volume. Which action best mitigates operational risk before launch?","choices":["Approve launch because average-volume testing passed.","Classify all future incidents as unavoidable market risk.","Use a formal new-product assessment including peak-load controls, dependencies and ownership.","Wait for the first regulatory finding before reviewing controls."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le lancement doit intégrer les risques de capacité, les contrôles, les dépendances et les responsables. Un test au volume moyen ne couvre pas les contraintes de pointe.","why":["Les pics peuvent faire échouer les contrôles.","Le mécanisme décrit est opérationnel.","Évalue le produit et ses contraintes avant exposition.","Une correction après constat laisse le risque ouvert."],"cue":"Tester les conditions du lancement réel.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b140","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-6.1","reading":"ORR-6","concept":"Audience-specific risk reports","question":"The board and a payment-operations manager receive the same 300-page incident spreadsheet. Which redesign is most appropriate?","choices":["Give the board the ticket-level repair schedule and operations only the aggregate loss ratio.","Give both audiences a total loss figure with no exposure or action information.","Send senior management only incidents already resolved, reserving open issues for operations.","Give the board an appetite-and-trend summary with escalation, and operations actionable detail."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le contenu doit servir les décisions de chaque niveau : surveillance et exceptions pour le conseil, causes et actions détaillées pour l’exécution.","why":["Inverse les besoins de supervision et d’exécution.","Un total ne permet ni surveillance des limites ni suivi des corrections.","Les problèmes ouverts et importants doivent aussi remonter pour surveillance.","Adapte le niveau de détail aux responsabilités."],"cue":"Adapter l’information à la décision.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b141","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-6.2","reading":"ORR-6","concept":"Dashboard trend distortion","question":"Reported losses fall while overdue high-severity issues and unresolved near misses rise. What is the best reporting conclusion?","choices":["The report should combine losses with forward-looking exposure and remediation indicators.","Risk has necessarily declined because realized losses fell.","Near misses should be ignored because they have no accounting loss.","The loss series should be replaced entirely by operating revenue."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Les pertes réalisées sont retardées et aléatoires. Les incidents évités, l’exposition et l’avancement des corrections complètent la lecture et peuvent signaler une dégradation.","why":["Combine les dimensions nécessaires.","Confond réalisation passée et exposition actuelle.","Les quasi-incidents peuvent signaler un contrôle fragile.","Le revenu ne remplace pas les indicateurs de risque."],"cue":"Croiser passé réalisé et fragilités présentes.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b142","topic":"operational","skill":"o-measure","objective":"ORR-6.3","reading":"ORR-6","concept":"Threshold changes in loss reporting","question":"A bank lowers its loss-collection threshold and incident counts double immediately. What should a risk report emphasize first?","choices":["The underlying incident frequency certainly doubled.","The definition change affects comparability and should be disclosed with like-for-like analysis.","The new data should all be deleted.","The loss severity of every event must have doubled."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le changement de seuil modifie le périmètre observé. Une série comparable à seuil constant et une explication de la rupture évitent de conclure à tort à une détérioration.","why":["La rupture peut être purement méthodologique.","Sépare changement de mesure et changement de risque.","Les nouvelles données restent utiles.","Un seuil de collecte ne double pas les pertes individuelles."],"cue":"Vérifier la comparabilité avant la tendance.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b143","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-7.1","reading":"ORR-7","concept":"ERM appetite translation","question":"A group states it has low tolerance for service disruption, but business units have no measurable limits. What is missing most directly?","choices":["A higher earnings target for the same teams.","A promise that all risk will be eliminated.","Translation into operational tolerances, ownership and escalation linked to strategy.","A rule that only external auditors may identify breaches."],"answer":2,"explanation":"L’appétit doit devenir utilisable : indicateurs, tolérances, responsables et escalade. Une formule générale sans déclinaison ne guide pas les décisions.","why":["Le profit ne précise pas la tolérance aux interruptions.","Le risque zéro n’est pas une politique réaliste.","Rend l’appétit opérationnel.","Les métiers doivent aussi surveiller leurs risques."],"cue":"Transformer l’appétit en décisions et limites.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b144","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-7.2","reading":"ORR-7","concept":"Economic versus regulatory capital","question":"A bank estimates internal economic capital above its regulatory minimum. Management proposes reducing the internal estimate to the minimum to reconcile the figures. Which response is best?","choices":["The two measures must always be numerically identical.","The regulatory minimum proves internal tail risk is zero.","Economic capital is defined as accounting equity.","Investigate their different objectives, scope and assumptions before deciding capital needs."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le capital réglementaire répond à des règles de supervision ; le capital économique exprime une mesure interne du risque. Des horizons, périmètres et niveaux de confiance différents peuvent expliquer l’écart.","why":["Les objectifs et méthodes peuvent différer.","Un minimum ne supprime pas les pertes extrêmes.","Le capital économique n’est pas simplement les fonds propres comptables.","Explique les différences avant une décision."],"cue":"Comparer les objectifs avant les montants.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b145","topic":"operational","skill":"o-model","objective":"ORR-7.4","reading":"ORR-7","concept":"Operational stress model extrapolation","question":"A stress model links legal losses to unemployment using only a short benign sample. What is the strongest challenge?","choices":["Sparse legal-loss observations and regime changes may invalidate the estimated stress relation.","A positive in-sample fit guarantees reliable tail extrapolation.","Operational losses never respond to the business cycle.","A larger coefficient always makes the model conceptually sound."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Les pertes juridiques rares, les délais et les changements de régime rendent l’extrapolation incertaine. Une revue conceptuelle et des scénarios complémentaires sont nécessaires.","why":["Identifie les limites d’échantillon et de régime.","L’ajustement interne ne valide pas la queue.","Des liens peuvent exister mais doivent être justifiés.","Le conservatisme apparent ne remplace pas la validité."],"cue":"Challenger les liens de stress hors échantillon.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b146","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-8.2","reading":"ORR-8","concept":"Cyber accountability","question":"A bank outsources all network monitoring and tells its board that cyber-risk accountability now belongs entirely to the supplier. What is the best response?","choices":["Accept the transfer because the contract is signed.","Retain bank governance and oversight of the outsourced cyber activities.","Let the supplier define the bank risk appetite unilaterally.","Eliminate the bank incident-response function."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Externaliser une activité ne transfère pas la responsabilité de surveillance. La banque doit conserver une gouvernance, des exigences et une capacité de réponse adaptées.","why":["Le contrat ne supprime pas la responsabilité de la banque.","Maintient la responsabilité et la surveillance.","L’appétit doit relever de la gouvernance de la banque.","Une réponse interne coordonnée reste nécessaire."],"cue":"Externalisation sans abandon de responsabilité.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d509.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b147","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-8.3","reading":"ORR-8","concept":"Cyber recovery testing","question":"A backup restores files successfully, but no test confirms that restored records are clean after a ransomware incident. What test is most useful?","choices":["Check only whether the server powers on.","Count backup files without opening them.","Test end-to-end recovery, integrity validation and delivery of the critical service.","Assume a faster restore proves data integrity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"La résilience vise le service fiable, pas seulement la disponibilité technique. Un test doit vérifier l’intégrité des données restaurées et la reprise de bout en bout.","why":["La mise sous tension ne valide pas le service.","Un inventaire ne confirme pas la qualité.","Teste la reprise fonctionnelle et l’intégrité.","La vitesse ne prouve pas l’absence de corruption."],"cue":"Reprendre un service correct, pas seulement un serveur.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d509.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b148","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-8.4","reading":"ORR-8","concept":"Actionable cyber information sharing","question":"Several banks detect the same new phishing infrastructure. Which sharing practice best improves collective defense while controlling disclosure risk?","choices":["Publish customer credentials with the warning.","Share only aggregate annual IT expenditure.","Wait until all institutions have suffered a loss.","Share timely technical indicators and mitigation information through trusted channels."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Des indicateurs techniques et des mesures de protection diffusés rapidement par des canaux de confiance permettent une défense coordonnée sans exposer les données sensibles.","why":["Expose les clients à un risque supplémentaire.","La dépense IT ne décrit pas la menace.","La prévention nécessite une information rapide.","Rend l’information exploitable et limite les divulgations."],"cue":"Partager une menace exploitable sans secrets clients.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d509.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b149","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-9.1","reading":"ORR-9","concept":"Credential theft and least privilege","question":"An attacker steals a junior employee password and reaches production customer records because all employees have administrator rights. Which control most directly limits this propagation?","choices":["Least privilege, privileged-access separation and strong authentication.","A longer annual financial report.","Higher credit limits for the employee clients.","Moving the same unrestricted access to another cloud provider."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le moindre privilège limite l’impact d’un compte compromis. Des accès privilégiés séparés et une authentification robuste réduisent les voies d’escalade.","why":["Agit directement sur l’étendue du compromis.","Ne limite pas les accès.","Sans lien avec l’accès système.","Déplace l’infrastructure sans corriger les droits."],"cue":"Limiter ce qu’un compte compromis peut atteindre.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d509.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b150","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-9.2","reading":"ORR-9","concept":"Patch assurance lesson","question":"A bank receives an urgent security patch notice. IT emails that the patch was deployed, but the vulnerable application is absent from the asset inventory. What lesson from major breach cases is most relevant?","choices":["An email confirmation alone is sufficient evidence.","Maintain a complete inventory and independently verify remediation on the affected assets.","Delete vulnerability notices after they are forwarded.","Focus exclusively on the cost of the patch."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Un inventaire incomplet et l’absence de vérification peuvent laisser une faille ouverte malgré une procédure formelle. La preuve doit porter sur les actifs réellement exposés.","why":["Une déclaration n’est pas un test de résultat.","Traite l’identification et la vérification.","Détruit la traçabilité.","Le coût seul ne démontre pas la correction."],"cue":"Identifier l’actif puis prouver la correction.","source":"https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/blog/2019/07/575-million-equifax-settlement-illustrates-security-basics-your-business","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b151","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-9.1","reading":"ORR-9","concept":"Social engineering payment redirection","question":"A treasury employee receives an urgent call apparently from the CFO requesting a confidential supplier-account change. Which control best resists impersonation?","choices":["Rely on the caller urgency as proof of authority.","Use only the telephone number supplied by the caller.","Independently verify through a pre-established trusted channel and require dual approval.","Bypass the approval workflow for senior executives."],"answer":2,"explanation":"La vérification par un canal préexistant évite de valider une identité avec les informations de l’attaquant. Une double approbation protège les modifications sensibles.","why":["L’urgence peut être un levier de manipulation.","Le numéro peut appartenir à l’attaquant.","Sépare la demande de la preuve d’identité.","Crée une exception exploitable."],"cue":"Vérifier hors du canal de la demande.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d509.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b152","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-10.1","reading":"ORR-10","concept":"Risk-based AML resources","question":"Two customer segments have equal account counts, but one has complex cross-border flows and opaque ownership. How should AML monitoring resources be allocated?","choices":["Equally by account count regardless of risk.","Only after a criminal conviction.","Only by customer profitability.","Using a documented risk assessment with enhanced measures for higher-risk exposures."],"answer":3,"explanation":"L’approche fondée sur le risque tient compte des clients, produits, pays et transactions. Le nombre de comptes ne suffit pas à caractériser l’exposition ML/FT.","why":["Ignore la différence de risque.","La surveillance est préventive.","La rentabilité n’est pas un critère suffisant de risque ML/FT.","Relie les ressources à l’exposition documentée."],"cue":"Dimensionner les contrôles selon le risque.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d505.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b153","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-10.2","reading":"ORR-10","concept":"Beneficial-owner verification","question":"A company provides incorporation papers but refuses to identify the natural persons who ultimately control it. What is the strongest due-diligence response?","choices":["Identify and verify beneficial ownership before accepting the relationship under applicable policy.","Treat the legal registration as complete beneficial-owner verification.","Accept because a company cannot pose money-laundering risk.","Replace due diligence with a higher account fee."],"answer":0,"explanation":"L’existence légale de la société ne renseigne pas les personnes qui la contrôlent. La vigilance doit couvrir le bénéficiaire effectif selon les règles applicables.","why":["Traite le point manquant de vigilance.","Confond existence juridique et contrôle ultime.","Les personnes morales peuvent servir à dissimuler des flux.","Un prix plus élevé ne corrige pas l’opacité."],"cue":"Distinguer société enregistrée et bénéficiaire effectif.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d505.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b154","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-10.3","reading":"ORR-10","concept":"Group AML legal constraints","question":"A foreign subsidiary faces privacy restrictions that limit transaction-data sharing with the parent. What should the group do?","choices":["Ignore the subsidiary because local law exists.","Assess the constraint, implement lawful compensating arrangements and escalate material limitations.","Secretly send all data in breach of local law.","Assume local compliance automatically satisfies every group risk need."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le groupe doit comprendre les limites, organiser des dispositifs licites et remonter les obstacles importants. Ni l’ignorance du risque ni la violation du droit ne constituent une solution.","why":["Abandonne la vue groupe.","Concilie droit local et maîtrise du risque.","Crée un risque juridique supplémentaire.","Des lacunes de vue groupe peuvent subsister."],"cue":"Documenter et traiter les limites de partage.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d505.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b155","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-11.1","reading":"ORR-11","concept":"Fraud control feedback","question":"A bank blocks many genuine transactions but misses a repeated mule-account pattern. Which change best improves the control framework?","choices":["Judge the system solely by the number of alerts generated.","Disable monitoring because false positives occur.","Use outcome feedback, typology analysis and independent testing to recalibrate monitoring.","Treat every alert as proof of criminal activity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Les alertes doivent être reliées aux résultats, aux schémas observés et aux contrôles de qualité. Leur volume seul ne mesure ni la détection réelle ni les coûts des faux positifs.","why":["Le volume n’est pas une mesure d’efficacité.","Les faux positifs justifient une amélioration, pas l’abandon.","Crée une boucle de validation et d’amélioration.","Une alerte appelle une analyse, pas une condamnation."],"cue":"Mesurer la détection utile, pas le bruit.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d505.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b156","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-11.2","reading":"ORR-11","concept":"Remediation assurance","question":"A bank repeatedly tells supervisors its transaction-monitoring deficiencies are fixed, but the same failures recur. Which lesson from enforcement cases is most relevant?","choices":["Closing an action in a tracker proves sustainable correction.","Increase alert thresholds solely to reduce the backlog.","Change the issue title to avoid recurrence statistics.","Validate remediation effectiveness, governance and sustainable operating capacity."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Les corrections doivent fonctionner durablement et être vérifiées. Des ressources, une gouvernance et des tests d’efficacité valent plus qu’une clôture administrative.","why":["La clôture administrative ne démontre pas le résultat.","Peut réduire la détection sans justification de risque.","Masque la récurrence au lieu de la traiter.","Vérifie la pérennité de la correction."],"cue":"Prouver la correction durable.","source":"https://www.occ.gov/news-issuances/news-releases/2022/nr-occ-2022-25.html","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b157","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-11.1","reading":"ORR-11","concept":"Fraud escalation conflict","question":"A relationship manager is allowed to suppress fraud alerts for profitable customers without review. Which redesign best addresses the conflict?","choices":["Require documented dispositions and independent review of overrides.","Let revenue targets determine whether alerts are investigated.","Delete alerts for long-standing customers.","Measure control quality only by processing speed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"La décision de neutraliser une alerte doit être motivée, traçable et soumise à un regard indépendant. La rentabilité du client ne remplace pas l’analyse du risque.","why":["Réduit le conflit et préserve la traçabilité.","Subordonne le contrôle à un objectif commercial.","L’ancienneté ne supprime pas le risque.","La vitesse seule ne mesure pas la pertinence."],"cue":"Contrôler les exceptions aux contrôles.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d505.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b158","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-12.1","reading":"ORR-12","concept":"Outsourcing concentration","question":"A bank contracts with three payment providers, all hosted in the same data center. Which conclusion is most appropriate?","choices":["Diversification should be measured by the number of independent contracts, without mapping hosting.","The shared infrastructure creates concentration risk despite multiple providers.","The lowest-cost provider should receive the highest concentration weight regardless of infrastructure.","The bank can treat provider outages as independent if each provider has its own service-level agreement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Des fournisseurs juridiquement distincts peuvent partager une dépendance critique. La diversification des contrats ne prouve pas celle des infrastructures.","why":["Les dépendances partagées peuvent dominer le nombre de contrats.","Identifie la concentration commune.","Le prix ne mesure pas l’exposition à une panne commune.","Des engagements contractuels séparés ne rendent pas les infrastructures indépendantes."],"cue":"Diversifier la dépendance, pas seulement les contrats.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2304.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b159","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-12.2","reading":"ORR-12","concept":"Vendor due diligence evidence","question":"A critical supplier has a strong sales presentation but refuses to show resilience-test results or financial information. What is the best due-diligence response?","choices":["Treat brand recognition as sufficient evidence.","Skip due diligence because the contract has an indemnity.","Obtain evidence proportionate to service criticality and assess unresolved information gaps.","Wait for the first outage before asking questions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"La diligence doit porter sur les capacités opérationnelles, la résilience et la viabilité du fournisseur. Les informations manquantes doivent être évaluées et traitées avant engagement.","why":["La marque ne prouve pas la capacité.","Une indemnité ne garantit pas la continuité.","Lie la profondeur de revue au risque du service.","La prévention intervient avant l’incident."],"cue":"Exiger des preuves de capacité.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2304.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b160","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-12.3","reading":"ORR-12","concept":"Exit provisions in contracts","question":"A bank can terminate a critical outsourcing contract in 30 days but has no right to retrieve its data in usable form. Which contract addition is most important?","choices":["A higher annual marketing budget for the supplier.","An automatic waiver of all audit rights.","A promise that no supplier will ever fail.","Data portability, transition assistance and tested exit arrangements."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Un droit de résiliation n’est utile que si une sortie opérationnelle est possible. La portabilité et l’assistance à la transition évitent une dépendance irréversible.","why":["Sans rapport avec la capacité de sortie.","Réduit la surveillance du fournisseur.","Une promesse ne remplace pas un mécanisme.","Rend la sortie réalisable."],"cue":"Une sortie doit fonctionner en pratique.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2304.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b161","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-13.1","reading":"ORR-13","concept":"Fourth-party dependency","question":"A critical vendor subcontracts identity verification to a small firm without notifying the bank. What risk-management gap is most evident?","choices":["Insufficient visibility and oversight of material subcontractor dependencies.","A vendor contract removes all subcontractor risk.","The bank now has no operational exposure.","The issue is solely the subcontractor share price."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Les dépendances en chaîne peuvent affecter le service critique. La banque doit disposer d’une visibilité et de dispositions adaptées sur les sous-traitants importants.","why":["Identifie une dépendance de quatrième partie.","Le risque subsiste au-delà du contrat direct.","Le service bancaire reste dépendant.","Le risque ne dépend pas seulement d’un cours boursier."],"cue":"Suivre la chaîne de dépendances.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2304.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b162","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-13.2","reading":"ORR-13","concept":"Case lesson on untested substitution","question":"A vendor-failure case shows that a nominal backup provider could not process the bank data format. Which lesson should be applied?","choices":["A second signed contract alone establishes substitutability.","Test data portability, capacity and end-to-end migration before relying on a fallback.","Rely on price comparisons to validate migration.","Use the same untested assumption in the next renewal."],"answer":1,"explanation":"La substituabilité doit être démontrée techniquement et opérationnellement. Un fournisseur de secours peut exister sans être capable de reprendre l’activité.","why":["Un contrat ne valide pas l’interopérabilité.","Teste les conditions réelles de transfert.","Le prix ne confirme ni format ni capacité.","Reconduit la cause de l’échec."],"cue":"Tester le transfert avant la crise.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2304.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b163","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-13.1","reading":"ORR-13","concept":"Risk tiering for third parties","question":"A bank applies identical one-page due diligence to office stationery suppliers and its sole clearing-service provider. What is the best redesign?","choices":["Assess all suppliers only by annual spend.","Apply the lightest review to the most complex service.","Tier relationships by criticality and risk, then adjust oversight and contingency planning.","Eliminate monitoring after contract signature."],"answer":2,"explanation":"La criticité, l’accès aux données, la substituabilité et l’impact d’une défaillance doivent guider la profondeur du dispositif, pas seulement le montant facturé.","why":["Une petite dépense peut soutenir un service critique.","Inverse la proportionnalité.","Adapte les contrôles au risque.","Le risque évolue pendant la relation."],"cue":"La criticité guide la surveillance.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2304.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b164","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-14.1","reading":"ORR-14","concept":"Suitability and conflicts","question":"A distributor recommends a complex leveraged note to a client with low risk tolerance because it pays the highest commission. Which investor-protection concern is most direct?","choices":["Only the issuer funding cost matters.","A higher promised yield eliminates the need to understand client needs.","The recommendation becomes suitable if the fee is undisclosed.","Suitability and management of inducement-related conflicts."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le produit doit correspondre au profil du client et les conflits liés à la rémunération doivent être maîtrisés selon les règles applicables. Le rendement affiché ne suffit pas.","why":["Ignore la protection du client.","Le profil et la capacité de perte restent essentiels.","La dissimulation ne corrige pas l’inadéquation.","Relie adéquation et conflit commercial."],"cue":"Client d’abord, commission ensuite.","source":"https://www.esma.europa.eu/publications-and-data/interactive-single-rulebook/mifid-ii","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b165","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-14.2","reading":"ORR-14","concept":"Investor disclosure case lesson","question":"A firm advertises an illiquid structured product as cash-like while burying loss and lockup terms in a long appendix. What lesson from compliance cases best applies?","choices":["Communications must present material risks fairly and clearly, not merely somewhere in the document.","Any appendix automatically cures a misleading headline.","Only historical return charts are relevant.","An investor signature removes all distribution responsibilities."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Une information essentielle ne doit pas être neutralisée par une présentation trompeuse. La clarté et l’équilibre de la communication comptent autant que la présence formelle du texte.","why":["Traite la qualité réelle de l’information.","La présence formelle n’efface pas le message trompeur.","Les pertes et l’illiquidité sont essentielles.","La signature ne justifie pas une présentation trompeuse."],"cue":"Vérifier le message réellement reçu.","source":"https://www.esma.europa.eu/publications-and-data/interactive-single-rulebook/mifid-ii","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b166","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-14.1","reading":"ORR-14","concept":"Best execution multidimensionality","question":"An execution desk always routes retail orders to the venue paying the largest rebate, even when client total execution cost is worse. Which assessment is best?","choices":["Largest rebate automatically means best client execution.","Routing should consider relevant client execution factors and manage the conflict from rebates.","Only the quoted commission matters; price and settlement do not.","Execution policy is unnecessary for small orders."],"answer":1,"explanation":"La meilleure exécution prend en compte les facteurs pertinents pour le client, notamment le coût total et les caractéristiques d’exécution. Les ristournes peuvent créer un conflit à maîtriser.","why":["Confond rémunération du courtier et intérêt client.","Replace l’intérêt client au cœur du routage.","Omet des dimensions déterminantes du résultat.","La petite taille n’annule pas l’exigence de politique."],"cue":"Évaluer le résultat du client.","source":"https://www.esma.europa.eu/publications-and-data/interactive-single-rulebook/mifid-ii","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b167","topic":"operational","skill":"o-model","objective":"ORR-15.1","reading":"ORR-15","concept":"Implementation error despite correct theory","question":"A validated pricing formula expects volatility in decimals. Production feeds 20 for a 20% volatility. Which model-risk source is most direct?","choices":["Only market risk; implementation cannot create model risk.","A failure of the underlying economic theory alone.","Incorrect implementation and unit handling.","A guarantee that the validation result remains applicable."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Un modèle théoriquement correct peut produire des résultats faux à cause de son implémentation. Les unités et la concordance des entrées font partie des tests essentiels.","why":["L’erreur informatique affecte les sorties du modèle.","La théorie peut être correcte ici.","Identifie l’erreur effective d’unité.","La validation doit couvrir l’implémentation utilisée."],"cue":"Tester les unités jusqu’en production.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b168","topic":"operational","skill":"o-model","objective":"ORR-15.3","reading":"ORR-15","concept":"Development documentation","question":"A developer reports excellent backtest results but cannot reproduce the training dataset or explain excluded observations. Which requirement is most directly missing?","choices":["A sufficiently large slide deck.","A decision to skip validation because performance is high.","A larger model coefficient.","Reproducible development data, documented choices and traceable implementation."],"answer":3,"explanation":"La traçabilité des données et des choix permet la reproduction et la contestation. Un bon résultat non reproductible ne suffit pas à soutenir un usage contrôlé.","why":["Le format ne remplace pas les preuves.","La performance déclarée ne dispense pas de validation.","La taille d’un coefficient ne garantit rien.","Rend les résultats auditables et contestables."],"cue":"Documenter pour reproduire et contester.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b169","topic":"operational","skill":"o-model","objective":"ORR-15.4","reading":"ORR-15","concept":"Validation beyond backtesting","question":"A model passes one historical backtest but is used for a new product with materially different optionality. What should validation prioritize?","choices":["Assess conceptual suitability, implementation and performance for the new use, including limitations.","Approve because the old backtest passed.","Use only the original developer assurance.","Validate only the model name, since the code is unchanged."],"answer":0,"explanation":"La validation porte sur l’usage prévu. Un nouveau produit peut sortir du domaine de validité malgré le même code et de bons résultats historiques ailleurs.","why":["Évalue l’adéquation à l’usage réel.","Le test ancien ne couvre pas nécessairement le nouveau produit.","L’avis du développeur ne remplace pas la contestation indépendante.","Un code identique peut être appliqué hors périmètre."],"cue":"Valider un modèle pour un usage.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b170","topic":"operational","skill":"o-model","objective":"ORR-16.1","reading":"ORR-16","concept":"Spreadsheet model inventory","question":"A spreadsheet converts expert scores into credit limits using numerical weights. Its owner says it is not a model because it has no machine learning. Which assessment is strongest?","choices":["Only machine-learning systems can be models.","A quantitative decision method can create model risk and belongs in the appropriate inventory.","Spreadsheets cannot affect financial decisions.","Manual input removes model assumptions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Un modèle n’exige pas d’apprentissage automatique : une méthode quantitative avec hypothèses et paramètres peut produire une décision et exposer la banque au risque de modèle.","why":["Le champ est plus large que le ML.","Reconnaît la méthode quantitative et son usage.","La feuille détermine ici une limite de crédit.","Les pondérations sont elles-mêmes des hypothèses."],"cue":"Identifier la méthode, pas l’étiquette.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b171","topic":"operational","skill":"o-model","objective":"ORR-16.2","reading":"ORR-16","concept":"Validation of vendor opacity","question":"A vendor refuses to disclose a model algorithm. The bank plans to use its output for material limit decisions. Which approach is best?","choices":["Vendor confidentiality eliminates the bank validation responsibility.","Accept all outputs because the vendor has many clients.","Assess available evidence, benchmark outcomes, document limitations and constrain use if understanding is inadequate.","Treat a licensing contract as proof of conceptual soundness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"L’opacité impose des mesures adaptées : compréhension suffisante, tests, comparaisons et limites d’usage. Une impossibilité de validation adéquate peut justifier une restriction.","why":["L’achat ne supprime pas la responsabilité de maîtrise.","La popularité ne valide pas un usage particulier.","Adapte la maîtrise à la limite d’information.","Le contrat ne valide pas le raisonnement du modèle."],"cue":"Acheter un modèle ne transfère pas son risque.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b172","topic":"operational","skill":"o-model","objective":"ORR-16.3","reading":"ORR-16","concept":"Case lesson on unit reconciliation","question":"A trading-loss investigation finds the same positions were valued by two systems using inconsistent notional units, and no one reconciled differences. What is the most useful model-risk lesson?","choices":["Different outputs always prove diversification.","All models should share the same unreviewed data pipeline.","The system producing the higher profit is necessarily correct.","Independent implementation checks and reconciliations must investigate material discrepancies."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Les écarts entre systèmes sont des signaux à expliquer. Des tests indépendants d’unités, de positions et de calcul auraient pu détecter l’incohérence.","why":["Les écarts peuvent être des erreurs.","Une dépendance commune peut masquer une erreur.","Le résultat avantageux n’est pas une preuve.","Rend les divergences observables et traitables."],"cue":"Réconcilier les écarts, pas choisir le chiffre préféré.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b173","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-17.1","reading":"ORR-17","concept":"Stress exercise interpretation","question":"A supervisor runs a common bank stress scenario to compare capital resilience. A bank calls the scenario the official forecast of the economy. Which correction is most appropriate?","choices":["Stress scenarios are conditional adverse assumptions, not necessarily forecasts.","The stress exercise guarantees no future losses.","A common scenario means all banks have identical business models.","Stress tests replace all capital planning decisions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Un scénario de stress sert à examiner une résistance conditionnelle. Il ne décrit pas forcément la trajectoire centrale ou la probabilité exacte de l’économie.","why":["Distingue scénario conditionnel et prévision.","Le test n’est pas une garantie.","Les expositions et modèles économiques restent différents.","Le stress informe la gouvernance et la planification."],"cue":"Stress n’est pas prévision centrale.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/stress-tests-capital-planning.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b174","topic":"operational","skill":"o-model","objective":"ORR-17.2","reading":"ORR-17","concept":"Coherent stress drivers","question":"A scenario combines a severe housing collapse with lower mortgage defaults and unchanged collateral values, without justification. What is the main design issue?","choices":["The scenario is too detailed to be useful.","Risk-factor and balance-sheet assumptions lack economic coherence.","Every stress scenario must assume all asset prices fall identically.","A severe scenario cannot include any judgment."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Les hypothèses doivent former une histoire économique cohérente ou justifier explicitement les exceptions. Des relations contradictoires peuvent minimiser artificiellement les pertes.","why":["Le problème est la cohérence, pas le détail.","Identifie la contradiction entre facteurs.","Les chocs peuvent différer selon les facteurs.","Le jugement est nécessaire mais doit être étayé."],"cue":"Raconter une trajectoire économique cohérente.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/stress-tests-capital-planning.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b175","topic":"operational","skill":"o-model","objective":"ORR-17.3","reading":"ORR-17","concept":"Balance-sheet dynamics in stress","question":"A bank assumes loan balances grow strongly through recession while funding costs, capital constraints and management actions remain unchanged. What is the strongest challenge?","choices":["A dynamic balance sheet cannot ever be modeled.","Revenue projections alone are sufficient.","Growth, funding, capital and management responses should be modeled consistently.","Static and dynamic assumptions always give identical results."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Une projection dynamique doit réconcilier actifs, passifs, financement et contraintes. Une croissance isolée peut créer des revenus sans coût ni capacité financière correspondants.","why":["La dynamique est possible si cohérente.","Les revenus dépendent du financement et des risques.","Relie les dimensions du bilan projeté.","Les hypothèses de bilan changent les résultats."],"cue":"Faire tenir ensemble bilan et financement.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/stress-tests-capital-planning.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b176","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-18.3","reading":"ORR-18","concept":"RAROC numerator reconciliation","question":"A project produces annual revenue 18, funding cost 7, operating cost 3 and expected loss 2, all in EUR m. Economic capital is 40. Define RAROC as net risk-adjusted annual income divided by economic capital, before tax. What is RAROC?","choices":["10%","27.5%","20%","15%"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le revenu ajusté vaut 18−7−3−2=6 M€. RAROC=6/40=15 %. La perte attendue se retranche du revenu ; le capital couvre une autre dimension du risque.","why":["Retranche un coût supplémentaire non donné.","Omet les coûts opérationnels et la perte attendue.","Omet la perte attendue.","Utilise tous les coûts et le bon capital."],"cue":"Définir le numérateur avant le ratio.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*(18-7-3-2)/40","value":15,"optionValue":15,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b177","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-18.5","reading":"ORR-18","concept":"Capital hurdle decision","question":"A project generates EUR 9m annual risk-adjusted income on EUR 60m economic capital. The required hurdle rate is 12%. Ignoring taxes and other constraints, what annual economic profit does it generate?","choices":["EUR 1.8m","EUR -1.8m","EUR 7.2m","EUR 9.0m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"La charge de capital est 60×12 %=7,2 M€. Le profit économique vaut 9−7,2=1,8 M€, donc le projet dépasse le seuil.","why":["Soustrait la rémunération exigée du capital.","Inverse le signe du surplus.","Donne la charge de capital seule.","Ignore le coût du capital."],"cue":"Soustraire le rendement exigé du capital.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"9-60*.12","value":1.8,"optionValue":1.8,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b178","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-18.7","reading":"ORR-18","concept":"Diversification allocation reconciliation","question":"Two units have stand-alone economic capitals 50 and 40. Group capital after dependence modeling is 70. A proposed allocation gives each its full stand-alone amount. What is the key issue?","choices":["The 20 diversification benefit should be added to each unit stand-alone capital before allocation.","The allocation sums to 90, so it does not allocate the 70 group total consistently.","Allocating 50 to the first unit automatically leaves 40 available from group capital for the second.","Assigning each unit half of the 20 diversification benefit would raise total allocated capital to 90."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Les capitaux isolés totalisent 90 alors que le groupe porte 70 après diversification. Une allocation cohérente du total doit préciser le traitement des 20 de bénéfice de diversification.","why":["Un bénéfice commun ne s’ajoute pas deux fois aux capitaux isolés.","Identifie l’absence de réconciliation.","Après 50 sur un total de 70, il ne reste que 20, pas 40.","Retrancher 10 de chaque montant isolé donnerait 40+30=70 ; le total ne resterait pas à 90."],"cue":"Réconcilier allocations et total du groupe.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b179","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-19.1","reading":"ORR-19","concept":"Aggregation of incompatible measures","question":"One desk reports one-day 99% VaR and another reports one-year 99.9% credit loss. Management adds the two and calls it group economic capital. What is the strongest objection?","choices":["Any two currency amounts are directly comparable.","Credit losses are never relevant to economic capital.","Horizons, confidence levels and risk-measure definitions must be reconciled before aggregation.","Adding them necessarily overstates every possible dependence structure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Les unités monétaires communes ne suffisent pas. Les horizons, niveaux de confiance, définitions et dépendances doivent être rendus cohérents pour donner un sens au capital agrégé.","why":["Le sens des mesures diffère.","Le crédit est un risque majeur du capital économique.","Traite la comparabilité avant l’agrégation.","Le sens du biais dépend des hypothèses."],"cue":"Même devise ne signifie pas même mesure.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b180","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-19.3","reading":"ORR-19","concept":"Risk-based customer profitability","question":"Customer A and B generate equal net revenue, but A consumes twice the economic capital. What does an economic-capital framework add to profitability analysis?","choices":["It makes the two relationships automatically equally profitable.","It proves customer A must always be rejected regardless of price.","It replaces all expected-loss estimates by zero.","It reveals different returns after charging for risk-capital usage."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Une charge de capital différencie les relations de même revenu mais de risque différent. Elle éclaire la tarification et la rentabilité sans imposer une décision unique hors contexte.","why":["Ignore le capital consommé.","Le prix, la stratégie et les contraintes comptent aussi.","La perte attendue reste pertinente.","Relie rendement et ressource de risque mobilisée."],"cue":"Comparer le revenu après charge de risque.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b181","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-19.4","reading":"ORR-19","concept":"Economic-capital model governance","question":"A desk changes its dependence assumptions to reduce allocated capital just before bonuses are set. What governance response is strongest?","choices":["Require independent challenge, documented approval and impact analysis before changes affect incentives.","Allow desk heads to approve their own methodology changes.","Freeze all models forever.","Judge the change only by whether bonuses increase."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Les hypothèses influencent les incitations et doivent être gouvernées. Une revue indépendante et une analyse d’impact limitent le risque de manipulation tout en autorisant une amélioration justifiée.","why":["Sépare intérêt commercial et validation méthodologique.","Crée un conflit d’intérêts.","Les modèles peuvent nécessiter des évolutions.","L’avantage privé ne valide pas la méthode."],"cue":"Gouverner les paramètres qui pilotent les bonus.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b182","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-20.1","reading":"ORR-20","concept":"Capital planning beyond minimums","question":"A bank capital plan simply projects compliance with current minimum ratios in the base case. What is the most important missing dimension of a robust capital adequacy process?","choices":["A promise never to issue capital.","Adverse conditions, material risks, capital policy and credible contingency actions.","A requirement to distribute all excess capital immediately.","A single revenue-growth target replacing risk identification."],"answer":1,"explanation":"La planification doit considérer les risques matériels, les conditions défavorables et des options de capital crédibles. Une conformité centrale ponctuelle ne suffit pas à juger la résilience.","why":["Réduit la flexibilité du plan.","Ajoute la vision prospective et la gouvernance.","Peut affaiblir la résilience.","Omet l’évaluation du risque."],"cue":"Planifier le capital sous conditions défavorables.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/bcreg20130819a1.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b183","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-20.2","reading":"ORR-20","concept":"RWA denominator in planning","question":"A bank holds projected CET1 constant at 12, while risk-weighted assets rise from 100 to 120 under stress. All values are EUR bn. What is the stressed CET1 ratio?","choices":["8%","12%","10%","14.4%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le ratio vaut 12/120=10 %. Le maintien du montant de capital ne stabilise pas le ratio si le dénominateur augmente.","why":["Utilise un capital non donné.","Conserve à tort l’ancien dénominateur.","Met à jour le dénominateur.","Inverse l’effet de la hausse des RWA."],"cue":"Projeter aussi le dénominateur du ratio.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*12/120","value":10,"optionValue":10,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b184","topic":"operational","skill":"o-govern","objective":"ORR-20.2","reading":"ORR-20","concept":"Credibility of contingency capital actions","question":"A stress plan assumes a large share issue during a market-wide crisis, with no investor analysis or execution lead time. What is the best challenge?","choices":["Any planned capital action should be assumed certain.","Treat an unapproved share issue as existing CET1 today.","Exclude all management actions from every analysis.","Assess feasibility, timing and market constraints; test alternatives if the action fails."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Une action de gestion ne produit du capital que si elle est réalisable au moment voulu. Le scénario doit considérer les contraintes et des solutions de repli.","why":["Transforme une intention en garantie.","Une émission projetée n’est pas du capital existant.","Des actions crédibles peuvent être pertinentes.","Teste la crédibilité plutôt que seulement le montant."],"cue":"Une action projetée doit être exécutable en stress.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/bcreg20130819a1.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b185","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-21.2","reading":"ORR-21","concept":"Historical Basel I RWA","question":"Under the simplified Basel I rules specified for this exercise, sovereign assets of 40 receive a 0% risk weight, residential mortgages of 60 receive 50%, and corporate loans of 100 receive 100%. All amounts are EUR m. Using an 8% capital ratio, required capital is:","choices":["EUR 10.4m","EUR 8.0m","EUR 13.6m","EUR 16.0m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"RWA=40×0+60×0,50+100×1=130 M€. Le capital requis dans l’exercice est 130×8 %=10,4 M€. Ce sont des règles historiques simplifiées explicitement données.","why":["Pondère les actifs puis applique 8 %.","Omet les RWA hypothécaires.","Applique une pondération non donnée.","Applique 8 % à tous les actifs sans pondérer."],"cue":"Pondérer avant de multiplier par le ratio.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"(40*0+60*.5+100)*.08","value":10.4,"optionValue":10.4,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b186","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-21.4","reading":"ORR-21","concept":"Basel II three-pillar purpose","question":"A bank argues that meeting Pillar 1 numerical capital requirements means supervisory review and market disclosure are unnecessary. Which response is best?","choices":["Basel II has only one pillar.","Supervisory review and market discipline complement minimum capital requirements.","Pillar 3 consists solely of internal audit.","Pillar 2 replaces every Pillar 1 requirement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Les trois piliers répondent à des besoins complémentaires : exigences minimales, revue prudentielle et discipline de marché par l’information. Le premier ne rend pas les autres inutiles.","why":["Le cadre prévoit trois piliers.","Reconnaît leur complémentarité.","La discipline de marché ne se limite pas à l’audit interne.","La revue prudentielle complète le minimum."],"cue":"Minimum, surveillance et information se complètent.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b187","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-21.8","reading":"ORR-21","concept":"Solvency II insurer perspective","question":"An insurer wants to assess its own solvency needs beyond a formulaic capital number. Which process is most aligned with the Solvency II framework?","choices":["A decision to ignore governance once the capital ratio passes.","A bank deposit-insurance premium calculation.","An own risk and solvency assessment linked to strategy and risk profile.","A guarantee that the standard formula fits every insurer perfectly."],"answer":2,"explanation":"L’ORSA relie le profil de risque, la stratégie et les besoins de solvabilité propres à l’assureur. Elle complète la mesure réglementaire plutôt que la remplacer par un simple chiffre isolé.","why":["La gouvernance reste nécessaire.","Concerne un autre dispositif.","Apporte l’évaluation propre à l’assureur.","Un cadre standard peut nécessiter une analyse des spécificités."],"cue":"L’assureur évalue ses propres besoins de solvabilité.","source":"https://www.eiopa.europa.eu/browse/regulation-and-policy/solvency-ii_en","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b188","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-22.4","reading":"ORR-22","concept":"Capital composition","question":"For this exercise, CET1=7, additional Tier 1=2 and Tier 2=3, with no deductions, all in EUR bn. RWA=100. What are the Tier 1 and total capital ratios?","choices":["7% and 9%","12% and 9%","10% and 12%","9% and 12%"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Tier 1=7+2=9 ; capital total=9+3=12. Avec 100 de RWA, les ratios sont 9 % et 12 %.","why":["Confond CET1 et Tier 1, puis omet Tier 2.","Inverse les ratios.","Inclut à tort une partie de Tier 2 dans Tier 1.","Respecte les niveaux de capital."],"cue":"Tier 1 inclut CET1 et AT1.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b189","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-22.5","reading":"ORR-22","concept":"Buffer versus minimum consequences","question":"A bank remains above its hard minimum CET1 requirement but falls into the capital conservation buffer. Which statement is generally most accurate under the Basel buffer design?","choices":["Constraints on distributions can apply even though the hard minimum is still met.","No supervisory or distribution consequence is possible.","The bank must automatically default on every liability.","The buffer is identical to a customer cash-withdrawal reserve."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le coussin de conservation ajoute une zone de protection au-dessus du minimum. Son utilisation peut déclencher des restrictions de distribution sans équivaloir automatiquement à une insolvabilité.","why":["Distingue minimum et contraintes de conservation.","Ignore la fonction du coussin.","Un franchissement de coussin n’est pas un défaut automatique.","Il s’agit de capital, pas d’encaisse de liquidité."],"cue":"Un coussin utilisé peut limiter les distributions.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b190","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-22.7","reading":"ORR-22","concept":"CoCo loss absorption","question":"A bank issues a contingent convertible bond that converts to equity if its specified capital trigger is breached. What is the intended loss-absorption mechanism?","choices":["It guarantees repayment at par after conversion.","Conversion increases equity capacity and exposes bondholders to equity risk at the trigger.","It removes all dilution risk for existing shareholders.","It functions only as ordinary secured repo funding."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le CoCo prévoit une absorption des pertes par conversion ou réduction selon son contrat. Ici, le déclencheur convertit la dette en fonds propres et modifie le risque des détenteurs.","why":["La conversion ne garantit pas le pair.","Décrit le mécanisme contractuel donné.","Une conversion peut diluer les actionnaires.","Le produit ne repose pas sur un nantissement repo ordinaire."],"cue":"Lire le déclencheur et le mécanisme de perte.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b191","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-23.1","reading":"ORR-23","concept":"Motivation for final Basel reforms","question":"Banks with similar portfolios report materially different model-based RWA. Which concern most directly motivates reforms aimed at comparability and credibility?","choices":["All portfolio differences are irrelevant.","Lower reported RWA always means lower true economic risk.","Excessive unwarranted RWA variability can weaken confidence in capital ratios.","A common framework must force identical profits at every bank."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Des écarts non justifiés par le risque rendent les ratios moins comparables et peuvent fragiliser la crédibilité des fonds propres réglementaires. L’objectif n’est pas d’effacer toutes les différences économiques.","why":["Les vrais écarts de risque restent pertinents.","Les modèles et choix méthodologiques peuvent influencer les RWA.","Identifie la variabilité indue.","Le cadre vise le capital, pas l’égalité des profits."],"cue":"Distinguer différence de risque et différence de méthode.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b192","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-23.2","reading":"ORR-23","concept":"Revised standardized operational approach","question":"A bank says its regulatory operational-risk capital must always equal its freely chosen internal AMA model estimate. Which assessment best reflects the revised Basel framework?","choices":["The revised framework leaves every bank free to choose any AMA formula.","The revised approach measures only credit-default losses.","Internal operational-risk models become useless for management.","The revised standardized operational-risk approach differs from a bank-specific internal AMA estimate."],"answer":3,"explanation":"La révision remplace les approches réglementaires antérieures par un dispositif standardisé. Des modèles internes peuvent rester utiles à la gestion sans définir à eux seuls l’exigence réglementaire.","why":["Ignore la standardisation du dispositif révisé.","Le périmètre est le risque opérationnel.","Un usage de gestion peut demeurer pertinent.","Sépare exigence standardisée et mesure interne."],"cue":"Séparer usage interne et formule réglementaire.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b193","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-23.3","reading":"ORR-23","concept":"Output floor binding calculation","question":"For this exercise, the applicable output-floor factor is 72.5%. Standardized RWA are 200 and pre-floor model-based RWA are 120, in EUR bn. Ignore transitional and other adjustments. What RWA apply after the floor?","choices":["145","120","200","265"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le plancher vaut 200×72,5 %=145. Le montant retenu est max(120;145)=145. Le facteur et l’absence de transition sont des hypothèses explicites.","why":["Calcule le maximum entre modèle et plancher.","Ignore le plancher contraignant.","Applique 100 % au lieu du facteur donné.","Additionne modèle et plancher."],"cue":"Un plancher est un maximum, pas une addition.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"Math.max(120,.725*200)","value":145,"optionValue":145,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b194","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-24.1","reading":"ORR-24","concept":"Operational standardized capital ingredients","question":"A bank has a business indicator component of EUR 800m and an applicable internal loss multiplier of 1.15. Under the exercise rule capital=BIC×ILM, required operational-risk capital is:","choices":["EUR 695.7m","EUR 920m","EUR 800m","EUR 1,150m"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le montant est 800×1,15=920 M€. Le multiplicateur s’applique au composant du business indicator selon la règle donnée, sans double addition.","why":["Divise au lieu de multiplier.","Multiplie les deux composantes.","Omet le multiplicateur donné.","Utilise 1 000 comme base non donnée."],"cue":"Appliquer le multiplicateur à la bonne base.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"800*1.15","value":920,"optionValue":920,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b195","topic":"operational","skill":"o-capital","objective":"ORR-24.2","reading":"ORR-24","concept":"SMA versus AMA model freedom","question":"Compared with an internal AMA regulatory approach, what is a key feature of the revised standardized operational-risk approach?","choices":["It permits unrestricted institution-specific regulatory loss-distribution formulas.","It eliminates the need to collect operational-loss data for risk management.","It uses prescribed business-indicator and applicable loss-data mechanics, reducing internal modeling discretion.","It excludes all large operational events by definition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le dispositif standardisé utilise une structure prescrite plutôt qu’un modèle réglementaire entièrement propre à chaque banque. Les données de pertes et les modèles restent utiles à la maîtrise du risque.","why":["Décrit la liberté que la standardisation vise à réduire.","La gestion conserve son besoin d’information.","Identifie le changement de structure.","Les grosses pertes sont importantes pour la mesure et le contrôle."],"cue":"Standardiser la formule, continuer à comprendre les pertes.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b196","topic":"operational","skill":"o-measure","objective":"ORR-24.3","reading":"ORR-24","concept":"Loss data event linkage","question":"A single operational incident creates litigation costs in year 1 and compensation payments in year 2. Why retain a common event identifier and detailed dates?","choices":["To treat every cash payment as an unrelated independent event.","To classify compensation as trading profit.","To delete all year-2 losses.","To preserve event aggregation, avoid double counting and distinguish event timing from accounting timing."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Un événement peut produire des charges à plusieurs dates. Les relier préserve la sévérité totale et permet d’analyser les délais sans inventer plusieurs événements indépendants.","why":["Gonfle artificiellement la fréquence.","La compensation n’est pas un profit de trading.","Les paiements ultérieurs restent pertinents.","Préserve l’unité de l’événement et sa chronologie."],"cue":"Relier les paiements à l’événement source.","source":"https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d515.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b197","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-1.1","reading":"LTR-1","concept":"Liquidity-adjusted liquidation VaR","question":"A EUR 20m position has a one-day market VaR of EUR 0.6m. The bid-ask spread is a constant 1% of mid and the entire position is sold at the bid. Define liquidity-adjusted VaR as market VaR plus half-spread liquidation cost. What is LVaR?","choices":["EUR 0.70m","EUR 0.60m","EUR 0.50m","EUR 0.80m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le coût aller simple est 20×1 %/2=0,10 M€. LVaR=0,60+0,10=0,70 M€, selon la définition fournie.","why":["Ajoute le demi-spread à la VaR.","Ignore le coût de liquidation.","Soustrait le coût au lieu de l’ajouter.","Ajoute le spread entier alors qu’une seule vente est prévue."],"cue":"Vente au bid : coût du demi-spread.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":".6+20*.01/2","value":0.7,"optionValue":0.7,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b198","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-1.2","reading":"LTR-1","concept":"Hedge margin and liquidity timing","question":"A commodity producer economically hedges future sales with futures. A price rise generates immediate margin calls while higher physical-sale receipts arrive six months later. Which risk is most direct?","choices":["The hedge guarantees no cash need at any date.","Funding liquidity risk from mismatched cash-flow timing despite an economic hedge.","The physical commodity has no remaining value.","Only an accounting classification issue with no financing effect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Une couverture économique peut créer un besoin immédiat de trésorerie si ses appels de marge précèdent les recettes de l’actif couvert. Le résultat final ne suffit pas à assurer la survie intermédiaire.","why":["Ignore les appels de marge.","Relie le besoin de financement au décalage temporel.","Le prix physique a au contraire augmenté.","Le décaissement crée un besoin réel."],"cue":"Résultat couvert, calendrier de cash non couvert.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b199","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-1.4","reading":"LTR-1","concept":"Liquidity black-hole feedback","question":"Many leveraged funds use similar volatility limits. Prices fall, measured volatility rises, and all funds sell into a thinning market. What mechanism best describes the amplification?","choices":["Independent sales restore depth without price effects.","A proof that market liquidity is constant.","Positive feedback between risk limits, forced sales and deteriorating liquidity.","A reduction of every fund leverage before any price movement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Les mêmes règles peuvent déclencher des ventes simultanées, réduire les prix et la profondeur, puis provoquer de nouvelles ventes. Ce cercle amplifie un choc initial.","why":["Les ventes corrélées peuvent réduire la profondeur.","Le scénario montre l’inverse.","Décrit la boucle auto-amplificatrice.","Le désendettement découle ici du choc."],"cue":"Une règle prudente isolée peut amplifier le choc collectif.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b200","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-2.2","reading":"LTR-2","concept":"Fractional-reserve transformation","question":"A bank funds five-year loans with demand deposits. Why can a solvent bank still face a liquidity problem?","choices":["Loan cash flows necessarily arrive before every withdrawal.","Demand deposits cannot be withdrawn during stress.","Solvency and immediate cash availability are identical.","Depositors can demand cash before loan assets mature, creating a timing mismatch."],"answer":3,"explanation":"La transformation de liquidité finance des actifs moins liquides par des engagements remboursables plus vite. Une valeur d’actifs suffisante n’assure pas la trésorerie au moment des retraits.","why":["Les échéances sont différentes.","La possibilité de retrait est centrale au risque.","Un bilan solvable peut manquer d’encaisse immédiate.","Identifie le décalage de liquidité."],"cue":"Solvabilité et calendrier de cash sont distincts.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b201","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-2.4","reading":"LTR-2","concept":"Balance-sheet leverage after repo borrowing","question":"A firm has assets of 100 and equity of 10. It borrows 20 in a repo and keeps the proceeds as cash, with no change in equity. Define leverage as total assets/equity. What is leverage after the transaction?","choices":["12x","10x","8x","14x"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le cash supplémentaire augmente les actifs à 120, les fonds propres restent à 10. Le ratio est donc 120/10=12 fois.","why":["Intègre le cash à l’actif et conserve les fonds propres.","Ignore l’expansion du bilan.","Réduit à tort les actifs du cash reçu.","Ajoute deux fois une partie du financement."],"cue":"Un emprunt conservé en cash gonfle aussi l’actif.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"(100+20)/10","value":12,"optionValue":12,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b202","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-2.7","reading":"LTR-2","concept":"Funding-market liquidity spiral","question":"A dealer collateral portfolio falls in price. Lenders also increase repo haircuts, forcing asset sales that depress prices further. Which interaction dominates?","choices":["The haircut increase always creates extra cash for the borrower.","Funding and market liquidity reinforce each other adversely.","Asset sales cannot affect future collateral capacity.","Only foreign-exchange settlement risk is present."],"answer":1,"explanation":"La baisse des prix réduit le collatéral et la hausse des haircuts réduit encore les fonds obtenus. Les ventes forcées peuvent aggraver les prix et le besoin de financement.","why":["Une hausse de haircut réduit le financement obtenu.","Décrit l’interaction entre les deux liquidités.","La capacité dépend de la valeur vendue ou conservée.","Le mécanisme ne repose pas sur un règlement de change."],"cue":"Prix, haircut et ventes peuvent former une spirale.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b203","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-3.1","reading":"LTR-3","concept":"Effective early-warning design","question":"A bank EWI flags funding stress only after its cash balance becomes negative. Which redesign is most useful?","choices":["Use only last-year accounting profit.","Lower the warning frequency to once every five years.","Use indicators with actionable lead time, calibrated thresholds and accountable escalation.","Remove thresholds so no breach can be recorded."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Un signal précoce doit permettre une action avant rupture : délai utile, seuils, responsabilité et escalade. Un indicateur constatant déjà l’échec n’est pas suffisant.","why":["Le profit historique ne décrit pas le stress courant.","Réduit le délai utile d’observation.","Ajoute capacité d’action et gouvernance.","Un signal sans seuil ni interprétation perd son rôle."],"cue":"Un signal doit arriver avant le besoin d’action.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b204","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-3.2","reading":"LTR-3","concept":"EWI supervisory expectations","question":"A treasury team monitors only its aggregate liquidity ratio and ignores deposit concentrations, rating triggers and collateral availability. What improvement is most aligned with supervisory EWI guidance?","choices":["Monitor market signals only after an internal cash-deficit trigger has been breached.","Keep the ratio as the sole EWI but present its compliant value more frequently.","Use budgeted funding expense as a complete substitute for concentration and collateral signals.","Monitor a range of institution-specific and market signals linked to funding vulnerability."],"answer":3,"explanation":"La supervision attend une surveillance multidimensionnelle des fragilités : concentrations, accès au financement, conditions de marché et déclencheurs contractuels. Un ratio ne couvre pas tout.","why":["Les signaux externes peuvent avertir avant le déficit de cash.","Une fréquence accrue ne corrige pas les dimensions de risque omises.","Un coût budgété ne représente pas la stabilité des sources ni la capacité mobilisable.","Élargit la surveillance aux canaux pertinents."],"cue":"Ne pas réduire les alertes à un seul ratio.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b205","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-3.3","reading":"LTR-3","concept":"EWI escalation before breach","question":"Wholesale funding tenors shorten rapidly, but no cash deficit has yet occurred. What is the best use of the warning?","choices":["Investigate drivers and consider earlier contingency actions under the escalation framework.","Wait until contractual payments fail.","Ignore it because total funding volume is unchanged.","Automatically assume the bank is insolvent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le raccourcissement des maturités accroît le besoin de renouvellement. L’alerte sert à analyser et agir avant la pénurie, sans conclure automatiquement à une insolvabilité.","why":["Utilise le signal pour une réponse proportionnée.","Arrive trop tard pour une alerte précoce.","Le volume masque le risque de maturité.","Une fragilité de liquidité ne prouve pas l’insolvabilité."],"cue":"Surveiller le tenor, pas seulement le montant.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b206","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-4.1","reading":"LTR-4","concept":"Security selection for liquidity buffer","question":"A bank must choose between a short Treasury bill and an illiquid private placement with a higher yield. The immediate goal is a readily monetizable reserve. Which factor should dominate?","choices":["Highest coupon regardless of trading conditions.","Marketability, credit quality and dependable monetization capacity.","The private placement label alone proves superior liquidity.","The longest maturity always produces the safest liquidity buffer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Une réserve mobilisable doit pouvoir être monétisée rapidement dans des conditions défavorables. Le rendement ne compense pas automatiquement une mauvaise négociabilité pour cet objectif.","why":["Privilégie le rendement au détriment de la fonction de réserve.","Aligne l’actif sur le besoin de liquidité.","Une dénomination ne garantit pas un marché.","Une longue maturité peut ajouter du risque de taux."],"cue":"Choisir la sécurité pour son usage de liquidité.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b207","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-alm","objective":"LTR-4.2","reading":"LTR-4","concept":"Bank securities concentration","question":"A bank already has large local mortgage exposure and proposes investing its reserve portfolio entirely in local property-linked bonds for extra yield. What is the strongest concern?","choices":["All securities have identical collateral eligibility.","A higher yield always improves diversification.","The reserve may lose value and liquidity in the same stress affecting the loan book.","Concentration matters only when assets share the same issuer name."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le portefeuille de réserve doit être examiné avec le reste du bilan. Une exposition au même facteur immobilier peut réduire sa valeur et sa liquidité au moment où la banque en a besoin.","why":["L’éligibilité dépend des actifs et des dispositifs.","Le rendement ne garantit pas la diversification.","Identifie la dépendance au même facteur de stress.","Un facteur commun peut créer une concentration multi-émetteurs."],"cue":"Diversifier les facteurs du bilan et de la réserve.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b208","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-alm","objective":"LTR-4.3","reading":"LTR-4","concept":"Barbell versus ladder maturity","question":"A treasury manager spreads purchases evenly across successive maturity buckets instead of concentrating at the shortest and longest maturities. Which maturity strategy is described?","choices":["A commitment to hold only perpetual securities.","A barbell strategy.","A strategy with no reinvestment risk at all.","A ladder strategy."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Une échelle répartit les échéances successives et organise les remboursements dans le temps. Le barbell concentre au contraire les positions aux extrémités.","why":["Aucune perpétuité n’est mentionnée.","Décrit une concentration courte et longue absente ici.","Les remboursements doivent toujours être réinvestis.","Décrit des échéances échelonnées."],"cue":"Échelle : répartir les échéances dans le temps.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b209","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-5.1","reading":"LTR-5","concept":"Net liquidity position","question":"For the next week, a bank expects deposits of 12, loan repayments of 8 and new borrowing of 5; withdrawals are 14, new loan disbursements 9 and other cash outflows 4. All figures are EUR m. Define net liquidity position as total cash sources minus total cash uses. It equals:","choices":["EUR -2m","EUR 2m","EUR 11m","EUR 25m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Les sources valent 12+8+5=25 et les emplois 14+9+4=27. La position nette est −2 M€, soit un besoin supplémentaire de liquidité.","why":["Soustrait correctement emplois et sources.","Inverse le signe.","Omet plusieurs emplois.","Donne seulement les sources."],"cue":"Sources moins emplois, avec le signe.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"12+8+5-14-9-4","value":-2,"optionValue":-2,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b210","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-5.2","reading":"LTR-5","concept":"Asset versus borrowed liquidity","question":"A bank can meet a temporary outflow either by selling securities at stressed prices or borrowing against eligible collateral. What trade-off should it assess?","choices":["Both choices have identical costs and future effects.","Realization losses and depleted assets versus financing cost, collateral encumbrance and rollover risk.","Borrowing against collateral never limits future funding.","Selling assets always leaves the future liquidity buffer unchanged."],"answer":1,"explanation":"La vente peut cristalliser une décote et diminuer la réserve. L’emprunt conserve l’actif mais ajoute coût, mobilisation du collatéral et renouvellement éventuel.","why":["Les conséquences diffèrent.","Compare les coûts et risques des deux stratégies.","Le nantissement peut réduire la capacité future.","La vente réduit l’actif disponible."],"cue":"Comparer coût immédiat et capacité future.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b211","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-5.3","reading":"LTR-5","concept":"Structure-of-funds estimate","question":"A bank has volatile deposits of 40, vulnerable deposits of 30 and stable deposits of 50, all EUR m. Policy reserves 50%, 20% and 5% of these respective categories as liquidity. Ignore all other needs. Required liquidity under this structure-of-funds rule is:","choices":["EUR 23.5m","EUR 35.0m","EUR 28.5m","EUR 60.0m"],"answer":2,"explanation":"La réserve prescrite vaut 40×50 %+30×20 %+50×5 %=20+6+2,5=28,5 M€. Les catégories ne reçoivent pas un taux uniforme.","why":["Omet une partie des réserves.","Applique une pondération non donnée.","Pondère chaque catégorie par son taux.","Prend 50 % de l’ensemble des dépôts."],"cue":"Pondérer chaque source selon sa stabilité.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"40*.5+30*.2+50*.05","value":28.5,"optionValue":28.5,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b212","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-day","objective":"LTR-6.1","reading":"LTR-6","concept":"Intraday liquidity source timing","question":"A bank has a securities sale settling tomorrow and a committed intraday credit line usable today. A payment is due in two hours. Which resource is directly relevant to meeting that payment on time?","choices":["Tomorrow settlement proceeds without bridge financing.","All future customer inflows regardless of timing.","The year-end accounting profit forecast.","The usable intraday credit line, subject to its conditions and capacity."],"answer":3,"explanation":"La disponibilité doit correspondre à l’heure du paiement. Une ligne mobilisable dans la journée peut couvrir le besoin ; un encaissement demain ne le couvre pas sans financement relais.","why":["Le cash arrive après l’échéance.","La date et la certitude des flux comptent.","Un résultat prévisionnel n’est pas du cash mobilisable.","La ressource est disponible au bon horizon."],"cue":"Vérifier l’heure de disponibilité.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs248.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b213","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-day","objective":"LTR-6.2","reading":"LTR-6","concept":"Intraday ownership and escalation","question":"Treasury assumes operations manages settlement liquidity, while operations assumes treasury does. An urgent payment fails. What governance improvement is most direct?","choices":["Define ownership, limits, real-time communication and escalation across treasury and operations.","Leave responsibility implicit to preserve flexibility.","Review only annual payment volumes.","Delegate all payment timing decisions to an unmonitored vendor."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le risque intrajournalier traverse les fonctions. Des responsabilités explicites, une coordination et une escalade évitent les angles morts entre suivi des paiements et financement.","why":["Organise la maîtrise transversale.","Maintient le défaut de responsabilité.","Le volume annuel ne résout pas les besoins horaires.","L’externalisation ne remplace pas la surveillance."],"cue":"Attribuer qui suit, qui finance et qui escalade.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs248.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b214","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-day","objective":"LTR-6.3","reading":"LTR-6","concept":"Peak intraday funding requirement","question":"Starting cash is zero. Sequential individual settlement cash flows are -8 at 09:00, +3 at 10:00, -7 at 11:00 and +12 at 16:00, in EUR m. A positive number is an inflow. What is the minimum extra opening liquidity needed to keep cash nonnegative throughout?","choices":["EUR 0m","EUR 12m","EUR 8m","EUR 15m"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Les soldes cumulés sont −8, −5, −12, puis 0. Le creux maximal est −12, donc 12 M€ de liquidité d’ouverture sont nécessaires.","why":["Regarde seulement le solde final.","Finance le déficit cumulé maximal.","Regarde seulement le premier paiement.","Additionne les sorties sans les entrées intermédiaires."],"cue":"Tracer tous les soldes avant de prendre le minimum.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs248.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"-Math.min(-8,-8+3,-8+3-7,-8+3-7+12)","value":12,"optionValue":12,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b215","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-7.1","reading":"LTR-7","concept":"Deterministic and stochastic cash flows","question":"A treasury forecast includes a fixed contractual bond coupon and uncertain customer withdrawals. Which distinction is most appropriate?","choices":["Both flows have identical certainty because they are in one forecast.","Withdrawals are deterministic solely because customers have accounts.","The scheduled coupon is deterministic under the contract; withdrawal amounts are stochastic.","No contractual payment can ever be forecast."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Une échéance contractuelle fournit un montant et une date déterminés sous l’hypothèse de paiement. Les retraits dépendent de comportements et nécessitent une distribution ou des scénarios.","why":["Le document ne rend pas les risques identiques.","L’existence du compte ne fixe pas le retrait.","Distingue engagement contractuel et comportement.","Le contrat donne une base de projection."],"cue":"Séparer calendrier contractuel et comportement.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b216","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-7.2","reading":"LTR-7","concept":"Liquidity option in commitment","question":"A bank gives a borrower an undrawn committed credit line. Why can the line be a liquidity option granted to the customer?","choices":["The bank determines all future drawdowns without customer choice.","The commitment is equivalent to cash already held by the bank.","An undrawn line has no possible cash-flow effect.","The customer can demand funding under the contract, potentially when the bank own liquidity is stressed."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le client peut exercer son droit de tirage. La banque doit prévoir le financement contingent, notamment si les tirages augmentent dans le même stress que ses propres besoins.","why":["Le contrat donne justement un droit au client.","Un engagement n’est pas une réserve de cash.","Un tirage transforme l’engagement en décaissement.","Identifie le financement contingent."],"cue":"Un droit client est un besoin contingent de cash.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b217","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-day","objective":"LTR-7.4","reading":"LTR-7","concept":"Cumulative maturity cash gaps","question":"Expected net cash flows for days 1, 2 and 3 are +4, -9 and +2, in EUR m. Starting liquidity is 6. Ignore any management action. What is cash available at the end of day 2?","choices":["EUR 1m","EUR -5m","EUR 5m","EUR 10m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Au jour 1, le cash passe à 6+4=10 ; au jour 2, il passe à 10−9=1 M€. Le flux du jour 3 ne peut pas couvrir rétroactivement le jour 2.","why":["Suit correctement le cumul jusqu’au jour 2.","Omet la liquidité initiale.","Inclut un flux futur ou inverse un signe.","S’arrête au jour 1."],"cue":"Arrêter le cumul à la date demandée.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"6+4-9","value":1,"optionValue":1,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b218","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-8.1","reading":"LTR-8","concept":"Dealer client-funding exposure","question":"A dealer provides prime-brokerage financing and clears derivatives for clients. Which liquidity exposure is most relevant across these activities?","choices":["Only the long-run dividend payout matters.","Client cash movements, collateral demands and margin requirements can generate rapid funding needs.","A dealer cannot face client-driven liquidity needs.","Clearing eliminates every cash-flow timing mismatch."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Les activités de courtage, de financement et de compensation créent des besoins de marge, de collatéral et de trésorerie liés aux clients. Leur rapidité est importante pour la gestion du dealer.","why":["Le dividende n’est pas le besoin opérationnel décrit.","Relie activités et canaux de cash.","Les clients peuvent retirer ou demander du collatéral.","La compensation impose aussi des délais et marges."],"cue":"Relier chaque activité du dealer à ses besoins de cash.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b219","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-8.2","reading":"LTR-8","concept":"Dealer franchise run","question":"Rumors cause clients to move balances away from a dealer while secured lenders shorten maturities. Which response is most credible before liquidity runs out?","choices":["Assume secured funding can never disappear.","Increase reliance on the same overnight lenders without a fallback.","Mobilize prepositioned collateral and execute tested funding actions while managing exposures and communications.","Use only a forecast of next-year profitability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Une crise de confiance peut toucher clients et prêteurs simultanément. Les actions doivent produire du cash à temps avec des ressources réellement mobilisables, tout en limitant l’amplification.","why":["Le caractère garanti ne garantit pas le renouvellement.","Accroît la concentration et le risque de renouvellement.","Mobilise des capacités préparées et gère la propagation.","Un bénéfice futur ne règle pas le besoin présent."],"cue":"Préparer la capacité avant la fuite des financements.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b220","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-8.3","reading":"LTR-8","concept":"Systemic dealer support versus solvency","question":"Authorities consider temporary broad-market liquidity facilities during a systemic funding freeze. Which qualification is most important?","choices":["Liquidity support automatically cures insolvency and all moral hazard.","A facility makes risk management unnecessary permanently.","Only individual dealers benefit; market functioning cannot be affected.","Facilities can ease funding dysfunction, but solvency, collateral, terms and incentives still require assessment."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Une facilité peut freiner une crise de liquidité et soutenir le fonctionnement du marché. Elle ne résout pas mécaniquement un déficit de solvabilité et doit être conçue avec des conditions et incitations adaptées.","why":["Confond cash temporaire et absorption des pertes.","La gestion du risque reste indispensable.","Une intervention peut agir sur le marché entier.","Distingue soutien de liquidité et contraintes restantes."],"cue":"Un soutien de cash ne remplace pas le capital.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b221","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-9.1","reading":"LTR-9","concept":"Restricted liquidity within group","question":"A subsidiary holds cash but local rules prevent transfer to the parent during stress. How should the parent treat it in a stress survival calculation?","choices":["As restricted liquidity unavailable to the parent unless lawful transferability is demonstrated.","As unrestricted parent cash because the group owns the subsidiary.","As a guaranteed parent inflow tomorrow.","As negative cash in all circumstances."],"answer":0,"explanation":"La vue consolidée ne suffit pas : la disponibilité dépend des contraintes juridiques et opérationnelles de transfert. Le cash local ne couvre pas automatiquement un paiement du parent.","why":["Tient compte de la restriction.","Confond propriété et accès effectif.","Ignore la contrainte décrite.","Le cash existe localement même s’il est indisponible au parent."],"cue":"Tester la transférabilité par entité.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b222","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-9.2","reading":"LTR-9","concept":"Usable liquid asset buffer","question":"A stress buffer contains cash of 10, unencumbered bonds worth 30 monetizable with a 10% haircut, and pledged bonds worth 20 that cannot be reused. All amounts are EUR m. What buffer is usable under these assumptions?","choices":["EUR 40m","EUR 37m","EUR 55m","EUR 60m"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le cash utilisable vaut 10 et les obligations libres produisent 30×90 %=27. Les titres déjà nantis non réutilisables sont exclus : total 37 M€.","why":["Omet la décote.","Exclut les actifs indisponibles et applique la décote.","Compte aussi les titres indisponibles avec décote.","Compte tous les titres sans contrainte."],"cue":"Disponible, libre de nantissement, après décote.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"10+30*(1-.1)","value":37,"optionValue":37,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b223","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-9.3","reading":"LTR-9","concept":"Combined liquidity stress design","question":"A bank stress-tests deposit withdrawals but assumes unchanged collateral haircuts and no commitment drawdowns during a market-wide shock. What is the strongest criticism?","choices":["Commitments cannot affect liquidity until year-end.","Every stress assumption must equal its historical average.","Combined stresses should consider correlated funding, collateral and contingent cash demands.","A stress test is valid only if no management action is allowed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Les mêmes conditions peuvent provoquer retraits, tirages et réduction de la capacité de collatéral. Négliger ces interactions peut sous-estimer le déficit de liquidité.","why":["Les tirages peuvent être rapides.","Le stress dépasse les moyennes usuelles.","Représente les effets conjoints plausibles.","Les actions peuvent être étudiées si leur faisabilité est justifiée."],"cue":"Tester ensemble les besoins et les ressources.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b224","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-10.1","reading":"LTR-10","concept":"Liquidity reporting actionability","question":"A liquidity report is delivered two weeks late and omits legal-entity constraints. Why is it inadequate despite accurate arithmetic?","choices":["Accuracy alone guarantees usefulness.","A delayed report always predicts future cash perfectly.","Liquidity reports should never include entity detail.","Timeliness, granularity and transferability information are essential for decisions."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Une information exacte mais tardive ou trop agrégée peut arriver après la fenêtre d’action et masquer un déficit local. La décision exige fraîcheur et granularité utile.","why":["Omet la date et le périmètre.","Le retard n’améliore pas la prévision.","Les contraintes par entité peuvent être déterminantes.","Relie le rapport à sa fonction décisionnelle."],"cue":"Bon chiffre, bonne date, bonne entité.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b225","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-10.2","reading":"LTR-10","concept":"Stock versus maturity-gap reports","question":"A bank has a large liquid-asset stock but faces a major payment tomorrow before expected inflows next month. Which report best complements the stock figure?","choices":["A maturity cash-flow ladder showing cumulative gaps by horizon.","Only the annual income statement.","A marketing customer-satisfaction table.","A report with all future flows netted into one timeless amount."],"answer":0,"explanation":"L’échéancier situe les déficits dans le temps. Un stock et un solde final agrégé ne montrent pas si la trésorerie sera disponible à la date précise du paiement.","why":["Ajoute la dimension temporelle manquante.","Le résultat annuel ne localise pas le déficit de cash.","Ne décrit pas le financement.","Le net sans horizon masque les besoins intermédiaires."],"cue":"Le stock répond combien ; l’échéancier répond quand.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b226","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-10.3","reading":"LTR-10","concept":"Stress report management-action dependency","question":"A bank survives a 30-day liquidity stress only if it sells a large illiquid loan portfolio on day 2 at par. What should the report highlight?","choices":["Only the final positive cash balance.","The reliance on that action, its feasibility, timing and sensitivity to sale discounts.","That every loan can always be sold at par.","That a positive modeled balance removes the need for escalation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"La conclusion dépend d’une action potentiellement irréaliste. Le rapport doit isoler cette dépendance et montrer ce qui se passe si la vente tarde ou subit une décote.","why":["Masque l’hypothèse déterminante.","Rend la conclusion interprétable et contestable.","Le prix et le délai de vente ne sont pas garantis.","Une fragilité de scénario peut justifier l’escalade."],"cue":"Montrer l’action dont dépend la survie.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b227","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-11.1","reading":"LTR-11","concept":"Stress tests into contingency actions","question":"A bank runs liquidity stress tests annually but its contingency plan has not changed after repeated earlier projected shortfalls. What link is missing?","choices":["A contingency plan should ignore modeled deficits.","The stress test must be replaced by an unchanged base forecast.","Stress results should inform triggers, funding actions, required capacity and plan testing.","Only the public-relations team should see stress results."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le stress doit alimenter les seuils, les actions et les ressources du plan de financement d’urgence. Sinon les résultats ne se traduisent pas en capacité opérationnelle.","why":["Coupe le plan des vulnérabilités.","Supprime l’analyse adverse utile.","Transforme le diagnostic en préparation.","La gestion et la gouvernance doivent agir."],"cue":"Chaque déficit de stress doit avoir une réponse préparée.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b228","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-11.2","reading":"LTR-11","concept":"Contingency plan operational detail","question":"A funding plan says only: borrow more if needed. What addition is most critical?","choices":["A requirement to wait for default before activation.","An assurance that all markets remain open.","A list of competitors office addresses.","Named responsibilities, trigger levels, executable funding sources, lead times and communication procedures."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Un plan doit être exécutable : qui décide, sur quel signal, par quel moyen et dans quel délai. Une intention générale ne fournit aucune capacité de réponse.","why":["Une activation après défaut arrive trop tard.","Suppose précisément l’absence de crise.","Sans rapport avec l’exécution.","Définit les éléments nécessaires à l’action."],"cue":"Qui, quand, comment et avec quelles ressources.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b229","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-11.3","reading":"LTR-11","concept":"Contingent funding double counting","question":"A contingency plan counts the same government bonds both as securities to be sold and as collateral for repo borrowing at the same time. What adjustment is needed?","choices":["Recognize mutually exclusive uses and avoid double counting monetization capacity.","Add both proceeds because the bonds have two uses.","Count the bonds a third time as unrestricted cash.","Ignore collateral identifiers in the plan."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Un actif ne peut pas simultanément être vendu et encore nanti par la banque. Les scénarios doivent préciser l’usage retenu et éviter de compter plusieurs fois la même capacité.","why":["Réconcilie les usages des actifs.","Confond possibilités alternatives et ressources cumulables.","Aggrave le double comptage.","La traçabilité aide à éviter l’erreur."],"cue":"Une même obligation ne finance pas deux actions simultanées.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b230","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-12.1","reading":"LTR-12","concept":"Non-deposit funding rollover","question":"A bank replaces retail deposits with overnight wholesale borrowing to fund the same long-term loans. Which risk generally increases?","choices":["The contractual maturity of the loans automatically becomes overnight.","Dependence on frequent market rollover and confidence-sensitive funding.","All liquidity transformation disappears.","Wholesale borrowing is guaranteed stable in every stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le financement court de marché doit être renouvelé souvent et peut se retirer rapidement. La maturité des actifs ne change pas lorsque le passif est remplacé.","why":["Le changement de passif ne réécrit pas les prêts.","Identifie le nouveau profil de renouvellement.","Le décalage de maturité demeure.","La stabilité doit être évaluée, pas supposée."],"cue":"Court terme de marché : renouvellement fréquent.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b231","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-12.2","reading":"LTR-12","concept":"Available funds gap","question":"A bank needs EUR 75m for new loans and securities. Available deposit inflows and other internally available funds total EUR 55m. Define available funds gap as funding uses minus those available sources. What is the non-deposit funding need?","choices":["EUR -20m","EUR 55m","EUR 20m","EUR 130m"],"answer":2,"explanation":"L’écart est 75−55=20 M€. Ce déficit doit être couvert par une autre ressource, une réduction des emplois ou une autre action adaptée.","why":["Inverse le signe du besoin.","Donne seulement les fonds déjà disponibles.","Calcule le déficit de sources.","Additionne sources et emplois."],"cue":"Besoin externe égale emplois moins ressources disponibles.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"75-55","value":20,"optionValue":20,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b232","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-12.4","reading":"LTR-12","concept":"Weighted historical funding cost","question":"A bank has EUR 80m of funding costing 2% annually and EUR 20m costing 5%. Ignore fees and reserve adjustments. What is the weighted historical annual cost rate?","choices":["2.0%","5.0%","3.5%","2.6%"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le coût annuel est 80×2 %+20×5 %=2,6 M€ pour 100 M€ financés : 2,6 %. La moyenne simple des taux ne respecte pas les poids.","why":["Ignore le financement à 5 %.","Ignore les 80 M€ à 2 %.","Prend la moyenne simple des taux.","Pondère par les montants."],"cue":"Pondérer les taux par les montants financés.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*(80*.02+20*.05)/(80+20)","value":2.6,"optionValue":2.6,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b233","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-13.1","reading":"LTR-13","concept":"Repo repurchase amount","question":"A dealer receives EUR 9.8m cash in a 30-day repo. The repo rate is 3.6% simple annual interest on an actual/360 basis. Ignore all fees. How much cash is repaid at maturity?","choices":["EUR 9.8294m","EUR 9.8000m","EUR 9.8353m","EUR 10.1528m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"L’intérêt vaut 9,8×0,036×30/360=0,0294 M€. Le remboursement est donc 9,8294 M€. Le haircut éventuel ne change pas la base cash déjà fournie.","why":["Utilise le cash et la convention donnés.","Omet l’intérêt.","Utilise environ 36 jours d’intérêt au lieu des 30 jours donnés.","Applique environ l’intérêt annuel au lieu de 30 jours."],"cue":"Intérêt sur le cash, selon la convention repo.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"9.8*(1+.036*30/360)","value":9.8294,"optionValue":9.8294,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b234","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-13.5","reading":"LTR-13","concept":"Special versus general collateral","question":"A bond is in unusually high demand for delivery, and borrowers of that specific bond accept a repo rate below the general-collateral rate. What is the best interpretation?","choices":["The lower rate proves the bond issuer is riskier than every GC issuer.","The bond is trading special because obtaining that security has value.","General collateral requires that exact bond identifier.","Specialness means the bond cannot be delivered."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Dans un repo spécial, le prêteur de cash recherche un titre précis et accepte un rendement cash inférieur. La rareté du titre crée l’avantage de financement pour son détenteur.","why":["Le différentiel décrit ici la rareté, pas nécessairement le crédit.","Relie le taux réduit à la demande du titre.","Le GC permet un ensemble de titres éligibles.","Le titre est recherché pour sa livraison."],"cue":"Un titre recherché procure un financement moins cher.","source":"https://www.newyorkfed.org/markets/treasury-repo-reference-rates","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b235","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-13.7","reading":"LTR-13","concept":"Financing advantage of special collateral","question":"A dealer can finance EUR 50m for 20 days at a special repo rate of 1.8% instead of a general-collateral rate of 3.6%. Use simple actual/360 interest and ignore fees. What is the cash financing advantage?","choices":["EUR 25,000","EUR 90,000","EUR 50,000","EUR 100,000"],"answer":2,"explanation":"L’économie vaut 50 000 000×(3,6 %−1,8 %)×20/360=50 000 €. Le spread de taux s’applique seulement à la durée de financement.","why":["Divise encore par deux le spread donné.","Utilise une durée ou une base différente.","Applique le différentiel et la durée.","Utilise le taux GC entier au lieu du différentiel."],"cue":"Avantage égale notionnel fois spread fois durée.","source":"https://www.newyorkfed.org/markets/treasury-repo-reference-rates","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"50000000*(.036-.018)*20/360","value":50000,"optionValue":50000,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b236","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-14.1","reading":"LTR-14","concept":"LTP governance and incentives","question":"Business units can choose their own liquidity transfer prices and exclude liquidity charges from performance reports. What is the strongest governance improvement?","choices":["Stop reconciling treasury and business-unit transfers.","Let each unit select whichever price maximizes its reported profit.","Use a zero charge for every maturity by default.","A centrally governed methodology with independent oversight and consistent allocation of liquidity costs and benefits."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Une méthode cohérente et gouvernée évite la subvention implicite et les arbitrages internes. Le dispositif doit rendre visibles les coûts et bénéfices de liquidité.","why":["Masque les transferts et incohérences.","Encourage la manipulation des résultats.","Ignore le coût du financement.","Établit cohérence et maîtrise des incitations."],"cue":"Le prix interne doit discipliner les décisions.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b237","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-14.3","reading":"LTR-14","concept":"Matched-maturity marginal LTP","question":"A five-year loan is funded internally at the bank overnight average cost even though five-year marginal funding is much more expensive. Which pricing approach best exposes the maturity-specific funding cost?","choices":["Matched-maturity marginal-cost pricing.","Zero-cost transfer pricing.","Using only last-year average deposit cost.","Charging every loan the same nominal fee regardless of tenor."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le coût marginal à maturité correspondante relie l’actif au prix de son financement de même horizon. Un coût moyen au jour le jour peut sous-tarifer la transformation.","why":["Reflète le terme et le coût de financement pertinent.","Supprime l’information de coût.","Mélange les maturités et le passé.","Ignore l’échéance et le profil de financement."],"cue":"Financer cinq ans ne coûte pas seulement une nuit.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b238","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-14.4","reading":"LTR-14","concept":"Contingent commitment liquidity charge","question":"A committed line has a EUR 100m limit and 40% stressed drawdown assumption. Treasury charges 1.5% annually on the required contingent funding capacity. Under this stated rule, what annual charge applies?","choices":["EUR 0.15m","EUR 0.60m","EUR 1.50m","EUR 4.00m"],"answer":1,"explanation":"La capacité à financer vaut 100×40 %=40 M€. La charge vaut 40×1,5 %=0,60 M€ par an selon la règle donnée.","why":["Utilise une base de 10 M€ non donnée.","Applique le taux à la capacité contingente.","Applique le taux au plafond entier.","Confond taux et fraction de tirage."],"cue":"Tarifer la capacité contingente à financer.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*.4*.015","value":0.6,"optionValue":0.6,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b239","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-15.1","reading":"LTR-15","concept":"Dollar shortage and maturity mismatch","question":"A European bank holds long-dated dollar assets financed with short-term dollar borrowing from wholesale markets. Those lenders withdraw during global stress. Why does a dollar shortage arise despite positive net asset value?","choices":["A positive dollar asset balance is sufficient because its accounting value measures same-day cash capacity.","The shortage is primarily an equity-capital calculation problem; the dollar maturity ladder adds little information.","Dollar liabilities mature before the dollar assets generate cash, and replacement funding is impaired.","Netting the dollar assets against euro cash in a consolidated report eliminates the need for dollar-market access."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le besoin est une disponibilité de dollars au bon moment. Des actifs longs et une valeur nette positive ne remplacent pas un financement dollar court qui ne se renouvelle plus.","why":["La valeur comptable ne garantit ni réalisation rapide ni absence de décote.","Le décalage de maturité en dollars est précisément le mécanisme de financement décrit.","Identifie le défaut de renouvellement dans la bonne devise.","Un net comptable ne réalise pas une conversion ou un transfert de devises."],"cue":"Devise et maturité doivent être financées ensemble.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/qtrpdf/r_qt0903f.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b240","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-15.2","reading":"LTR-15","concept":"Consolidation masks currency gap","question":"A group report nets a EUR cash surplus in one subsidiary against a USD shortfall in another, ignoring transfer restrictions and FX market access. What is the strongest objection?","choices":["Consolidation guarantees frictionless currency conversion.","Every cash surplus is legally trapped forever.","Only the group total number can be relevant.","Entity, currency and maturity mismatches must be assessed rather than netted away mechanically."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le total consolidé peut masquer des déficits de devise ou d’entité. L’analyse doit démontrer la possibilité de transfert, de conversion et la compatibilité des échéances.","why":["Les frictions persistent malgré la consolidation.","Les restrictions varient et doivent être vérifiées.","Un paiement local doit être financé localement en temps utile.","Rétablit les dimensions pertinentes du financement."],"cue":"Ne pas effacer les écarts par une consolidation comptable.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/qtrpdf/r_qt0903f.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b241","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-15.3","reading":"LTR-15","concept":"Central-bank dollar swap line function","question":"During a dollar funding squeeze, a central bank obtains dollars through a swap line and lends dollars to local banks against eligible collateral. What channel is intended?","choices":["Distribution of temporary dollar liquidity where private dollar funding is impaired.","Permanent cancellation of all private dollar debts.","A guaranteed increase in every bank equity.","Conversion of all local assets into US government bonds."],"answer":0,"explanation":"La ligne facilite l’accès temporaire à la liquidité en dollars via la banque centrale locale. Elle ne supprime pas la dette ni le besoin d’évaluer le risque et le collatéral.","why":["Décrit la transmission du financement en devise.","Une facilité de liquidité n’est pas une remise de dette.","Un prêt de cash n’est pas du capital social.","Aucune conversion de tous les actifs n’est nécessaire."],"cue":"Fournir la devise manquante, temporairement.","source":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/central-bank-liquidity-swaps.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b242","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-16.1","reading":"LTR-16","concept":"FX swap versus cross-currency swap","question":"A treasurer exchanges two currencies at spot and reverses the principal exchange at a pre-agreed forward rate, with no periodic coupon exchanges. Which instrument is described?","choices":["A cross-currency interest-rate swap with periodic coupon exchanges.","An FX swap.","A single unsecured domestic deposit.","An equity total-return swap."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Un FX swap combine un échange spot et son échange inverse à terme. Un cross-currency swap comporte généralement des flux d’intérêts périodiques sur une durée plus longue.","why":["Ajoute des coupons absents du contrat donné.","Correspond aux deux échanges de principal décrits.","Une seule devise et aucun échange inverse ne conviennent pas.","Aucun rendement d’action n’est échangé."],"cue":"Spot plus terme inverse : FX swap.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/qtrpdf/r_qt1609e.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b243","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-16.2","reading":"LTR-16","concept":"Basis from one-sided funding demand","question":"Many institutions seek dollar funding through FX swaps while dealer balance sheets are constrained. Which outcome is most plausible?","choices":["The basis can change only if a sovereign formally defaults.","The basis must be zero regardless of market constraints.","Persistent pressure on the cross-currency basis reflecting funding demand and intermediation costs.","Every FX swap becomes an outright currency bet without a reverse exchange."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Une demande déséquilibrée de financement en devise et des contraintes de bilan peuvent empêcher l’arbitrage de ramener immédiatement la base à zéro.","why":["Le défaut souverain n’est pas le seul canal.","Ignore les contraintes de marché.","Relie prix de base et capacité d’intermédiation.","La structure contractuelle du swap ne disparaît pas."],"cue":"La base reflète aussi le coût du bilan intermédiaire.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/qtrpdf/r_qt1609e.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b244","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-funding","objective":"LTR-16.3","reading":"LTR-16","concept":"CIP deviations and arbitrage capacity","question":"An analyst observes a covered-interest-parity deviation and concludes there is unlimited costless profit for any bank. Which qualification is most important?","choices":["Use only quoted deposit rates; dealer balance-sheet charges need not enter an executable arbitrage comparison.","Treat the observed deviation as evidence that the investor must take an unhedged currency position.","Scale the quoted trade without limit because covering exchange risk also removes liquidity constraints.","Hedged arbitrage can require funding, capital, collateral and scarce balance-sheet capacity."],"answer":3,"explanation":"L’arbitrage couvert exige des transactions et des ressources réelles. Coûts de financement, contraintes de bilan, limites et prix exécutables peuvent maintenir une base.","why":["Les coûts et contraintes d’intermédiation influencent le profit réalisable.","Un montage couvert peut rester limité par le financement et les coûts de bilan.","La couverture du change ne supprime ni limites de volume ni besoin de cash.","Intègre les limites concrètes à l’arbitrage."],"cue":"Sans risque de change ne signifie pas sans coût de bilan.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/qtrpdf/r_qt1609e.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b245","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-alm","objective":"LTR-17.2","reading":"LTR-17","concept":"Repricing gap and annual NII","question":"Over the next year, EUR 80m of assets and EUR 110m of liabilities reprice immediately and fully by a parallel +1% rate shock. Assume balances stay fixed and ignore all other effects. Approximate annual NII change is:","choices":["EUR -0.30m","EUR +0.30m","EUR -1.10m","EUR +0.80m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le gap est 80−110=−30 M€. La variation de NII vaut −30×1 %=−0,30 M€ avec les hypothèses de repricing immédiat et intégral.","why":["Applique le signe du gap.","Inverse le signe.","Compte les passifs sans les actifs.","Compte les actifs sans les passifs."],"cue":"Hausse des taux : signe du gap de repricing.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"(80-110)*.01","value":-0.3,"optionValue":-0.3,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b246","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-alm","objective":"LTR-17.3","reading":"LTR-17","concept":"Duration gap and equity value","question":"A bank has assets A=200, liabilities L=180, asset duration 4 and liability duration 2. Use ΔE≈−[DA×A−DL×L]×Δy/(1+y), with y=10% and Δy=+1%. Amounts are EUR m. What is approximate equity-value change?","choices":["EUR +4.0m","EUR -4.0m","EUR -4.4m","EUR -8.0m"],"answer":1,"explanation":"La sensibilité nette est 4×200−2×180=440. Le changement vaut −440×0,01/1,10=−4 M€. La valeur des actifs baisse davantage que celle des passifs.","why":["Inverse le signe de la hausse des taux.","Applique le montant net et l’ajustement de rendement.","Omet la division par 1+y.","Omet la sensibilité des passifs et l’ajustement."],"cue":"Valeur des fonds propres : sensibilité actif moins passif.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"-(4*200-2*180)*.01/1.1","value":-4,"optionValue":-4,"tolerance":1e-05}},{"id":"b247","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-alm","objective":"LTR-17.4","reading":"LTR-17","concept":"Gap management limitations","question":"A bank reports zero one-year repricing gap and claims it has eliminated all interest-rate risk. Which qualification is strongest?","choices":["Equal bucket totals guarantee a zero duration gap.","A zero gap proves every cash flow reprices on the same date.","A zero bucket gap does not capture within-bucket timing, basis changes, deposit behavior or embedded options.","Interest-rate risk can exist only when accounting equity is negative."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Des montants égaux dans une tranche ne garantissent ni dates identiques ni transmissions de taux identiques. La base, les comportements et les options peuvent créer des risques résiduels.","why":["La durée dépend de tous les flux, pas seulement du bucket.","Les dates précises peuvent différer.","Identifie les limites de l’agrégation.","La solvabilité comptable n’est pas la condition d’existence du risque."],"cue":"Un gap nul n’est pas un bilan sans risque de taux.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs144.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b248","topic":"liquidity","skill":"l-metrics","objective":"ORR-22.6","reading":"ORR-22","concept":"LCR cap and denominator","question":"For this exercise, eligible HQLA after all adjustments are 90. Thirty-day cash outflows are 120 and contractual inflows are 110, all EUR m. Recognized inflows are capped at 75% of outflows. Define LCR=HQLA/net cash outflows. What is LCR?","choices":["75%","100%","900%","300%"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Les entrées reconnues valent min(110;0,75×120)=90. Les sorties nettes sont 120−90=30. Le ratio vaut 90/30=300 %. Le plafond est explicitement donné.","why":["Divise par les sorties brutes.","Ne calcule pas les sorties nettes.","Utilise toutes les entrées sans plafond.","Applique le plafond puis le bon dénominateur."],"cue":"Plafonner les entrées avant de calculer le ratio.","source":"https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/standard/LCR.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"100*90/(120-Math.min(110,.75*120))","value":300,"optionValue":300,"tolerance":1e-05}}];
